      "text": "522,083,034? Wait, but the user says the correct answer is 522,013,034. Hmm, there's a discrepancy here. I must have made a mistake in the calculation steps.\n\nWait let me recheck each step carefully.\n\nLet me write down each digit's place step by step.\n\nFirst number: 351,943,250.\n\nBreaking down each digit from right (ones) to left (hundred millions):\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 0.\n\n2 (tens):5.\n\n3 (hundreds):2.\n\n4 (thousands):3.\n\n5 (ten thousands):4.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):9.\n\n7 (millions):1.\n\n8 (ten millions):5.\n\n9 (hundred millions):3.\n\nSecond number:170,139,784.\n\nBreaking down similarly:\n\nPosition1 (ones):4.\n\n2 (tens):8.\n\n3 (hundreds):7.\n\n4 (thousands):9.\n\n5 (ten thousands):3.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):1.\n\n7 (millions):0.\n\n8 (ten millions):7.\n\n9 (hundred millions):1.\n\nNow adding each position from right to left, keeping track of carryover:\n\nStart at position1 (ones):\n\n0 +4 =4. No carryover. Digit1:4.\n\nPosition2 (tens):\n\n5 +8 =13. Write 3, carryover 1. Digit2:3, carryover=1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):\n\n2 +7 +1 (carryover)=10. Write 0, carryover1. Digit3:0, carryover1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):\n\n3 +9 +1 (carryover)=13. Write3, carryover1. Digit4:3, carryover1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):\n\n4 +3 +1 (carryover)=8. Write8, no carryover. Digit5:8, carryover0.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):\n\n9 +1=10. Write0, carryover1. Digit6:0, carryover1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):\n\n1 (from first number) +0 (second's millions) +1 (carryover)=2. Write2, no carryover. Digit7:2.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):\n\n5 (first) +7 (second) =12. Write2, carryover1. Digit8:2, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):\n\n3 +1 +1 (carryover)=5. Write5. Digit9:5.\n\nSo the digits from position9 to position1 are:5 (hundred millions),2 (ten millions),2 (millions),0 (hundred thousands),8 (ten thousands),3 (thousands),0 (hundreds),3 (tens),4 (ones).\n\nWait, but the millions place is position7, which is 2. So putting all together:\