ing each position starting from position1:\n\nPosition1:6 +1 =7. No carryover. Result digit:7.\n\nPosition2:5 +7=12. Result:2, carryover1.\n\nPosition3:4 +8=12 +1=13. Result:3, carryover1.\n\nPosition4:2 +3=5 +1=6. Result:6, carryover0.\n\nPosition5:0 +6=6. Result:6, carryover0.\n\nPosition6:0 +0=0. Result:0, carryover0.\n\nPosition7:6 +4=10. Result:0, carryover1.\n\nPosition8:9 +6=15 +1(carryover)=16. Result:6, carryover1.\n\nPosition9:7 +8=15 +1(carryover)=16. Result:6, carryover1.\n\nNow, the carryover after position9 is 1, so we add a new digit (position10) as 1.\n\nNow, compiling the result digits from position1 to position10:\n\nPosition10:1\n\nPosition9:6\n\nPosition8:6\n\nPosition7:0\n\nPosition6:0\n\nPosition5:6\n\nPosition4:6\n\nPosition3:3\n\nPosition2:2\n\nPosition1:7\n\nSo the number is:\n\nPosition10 (billions):1,\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):6,\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):6,\n\nPosition7 (millions):0,\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):0,\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):6,\n\nPosition4 (thousands):6,\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):3,\n\nPosition2 (tens):2,\n\nPosition1 (ones):7.\n\nPutting them together from left (billions) to right (ones):\n\n1 6 6 0 0 6 6 3 2 7\n\nWhich is 1,660,066,327.\n\nBut the user's answer is 1,660,063,327. The difference is in the thousands place. In my calculation, it's 6 (position4), but the user has 3 there?\n\nWait, let's check position4 again. Position4 is thousands place.\n\nOriginal digits:\n\nFirst number's thousands digit (position4):2\n\nSecond number's thousands digit (position4):3\n\nAdding them:2+3=5, plus carryover from position3 (which was 1). Wait, wait no. Wait, the carryover from position3 (hundreds place) is 1. Let me check again.\n\nWait, position3 is hundreds place. The addition there was 4+8=12 plus carryover1? Wait no:\n\nWait, Position3 is hundreds place. The digits are 4 (first number) and 8 (second number). So 4+8=12, plus carryover from position2 (which was 1). So total 13. So the carryover to position4 is 1