nWait, but let me list them in order:.\n\nThe result digits are:.\n\nPosition1 (ones):0.\n\nPosition2 (tens):0.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):4.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):7.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):6.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):9.\n\nPosition7 (millions):7 (from 17 here? Wait, position7 was 9+8=17, so we write 7 and carryover1 to next position.\n\nWait, position7 is millions place. The sum here was 9 (from first number) +8 (second number) =17. So write 7, carryover1 to the next (ten millions place).\n\nThen position8 (ten millions): original digits 1 +6=7 plus the carryover1 makes 8. So that's correct.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions): 1+2=3, no carryover.\n\nWait, so the digits from position1 to position9 are:.\n\n0,0,4,7,6,9,7,8,3. So writing them in order from highest to lowest place:.\n\nHundred millions (position9):3.\n\nTen millions (8):8.\n\nMillions (7):7.\n\nHundred thousands (6):9.\n\nTen thousands (5):6.\n\nThousands (4):7.\n\nHundreds (3):4.\n\nTens (2):0.\n\nOnes (1):0</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
