      "text": "1,138,556,375? Wait, but the user said the correct answer is 1,136,556,375. Hmm, there's a discrepancy here. Let me check again step by step.\n\nWait, let me recalculate each column carefully:\n\nLet me list each place with their digits and the carryover step by step:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\n1. Ones place:\n   First number:7\n   Second number:8\n   Sum:7+8=15 \u2192 write 5, carryover 1.\n\n2. Tens place:\n   First number:7\n   Second number:9\n   Sum:7+9=16 + carryover1 \u219217 \u2192 write7, carryover1.\n\n3. Hundreds place:\n   First number:7\n   Second number:5\n   Sum:7+5=12 +1=13 \u2192 write3, carryover1.\n\n4. Thousands place:\n   First number:9\n   Second number:6\n   Sum:9+6=15 +1=16 \u2192 write6, carryover1.\n\n5. Ten thousands place:\n   First number:6\n   Second number:8\n   Sum:6+8=14 +1=15 \u2192 write5, carryover1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:\n   First number:2\n   Second number:2\n   Sum:2+2=4 +1=5 \u2192 write5, carryover0.\n\n7. Millions place:\n   First number:7\n   Second number:1\n   Sum:7+1=8 \u2192 write8, carryover0.\n\n8. Ten millions place:\n   First number:3\n   Second number:0\n   Sum:3+0=3 \u2192 write3, carryover0.\n\n9. Hundred millions place:\n   First number:6\n   Second number:5\n   Sum:6+5=11 \u2192 write11, carryover1 to the next (billions) place.\n\nWait, but the hundred millions place can only hold a single digit, so actually, the 11 here means we need to carry over 1 to the billions place. So the actual digits would be:\n\n- Billions place:1 (from the carryover)\n- Hundred millions place:1 (from 11-10)\n- Then the rest as above.\n\nSo putting all digits together from highest to lowest:\n\nBillions place:1\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nTen millions:3\n\nMillions:8\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nTen thousands:5\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:3\n\nTens:7\n\nOnes:5\n\nSo combining these digits: 1,138,556,375.\n\nBut the user's answer is 1,136,556,375. Hmm, so where did I go wrong?\n\nWait let me check