usands place: 3 + 6 = 9\n6. The hundred thousands place: 9 + 6 = 15 (write down 5, carry over 1)\n7. The millions place: 0 + 5 + 1 (carry) = 6\n8. The ten millions place: 2 + 1 = 3\n9. The hundred millions place: 3 + 7 = 10 (write down 0, carry over 1)\n10. The billions place: 1 (carry over)\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is 1,036,599,997.\n\nWait but the user\'s answer was 1,036,599,996. So there\'s a discrepancy. Maybe I should mention that the correct answer is different from what the user thought, but follow the template as per instructions.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made a mistake in counting the places. Let me confirm once more.\n\nWait the two numbers:\n\nFirst number:320,935,006\n\nSecond number:715,664,991\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me add using another method. Let\'s write them as:\n\n320,935,006\n\n+715,664,991\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n6 +1 =7\n\n0+9=9\n\n0+9=9\n\n5+4=9\n\n3+6=9\n\n9+6=15 (carry 1)\n\n0+5+1=6\n\n2+1=3\n\n3+7=10 (carry 1)\n\n0 (since no higher digits except the carry) plus the carry makes 1.\n\nSo the total is 1,036,599,997. So that\'s correct. The user\'s answer is 1,036,599,996, which is one less. The mistake is probably in the ones place, where they added 6+1 and got 6 instead of 7. So that\'s where the error is.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be 1,036,599,997. I\'ll proceed to write that in the template.\n</think>', '']  8%|8         | 41/500 [1:40:58<14:56:54, 117.24s/it]
