ands), 4 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 5 (ones). .\n\nWait, so for the millions place, the first number has 9 (since it's the millions digit), and the second has 9 as well? Let me confirm. Let's parse each digit step by step:.\n\nFirst number: 589,473,790.\n- Positions from right (starting at 1):.\n1: 0 (ones).\n2: 9 (tens).\n3: 7 (hundreds).\n4: 3 (thousands).\n5: 7 (ten thousands).\n6: 4 (hundred thousands).\n7: 9 (millions).\n8: 8 (ten millions).\n9: 5 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 219,574,375.\n- Positions from right:.\n1:5.\n2:7.\n3:3.\n4:4.\n5:7.\n6:5.\n7:9.\n8:1.\n9:2.\n\nSo, when adding, the millions place (position 7 from the right, which is the 7th digit) for the first number is 9, and for the second number it's 9. So 9+9=18. Wait, but earlier I thought the hundred-thousands place? Maybe I got confused with the place names. Let me re-express the numbers with place values properly.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps it's easier to write each number digit by digit, separated by commas for clarity. Let's list each digit from right to left (since addition starts from the right):.\n\nFirst number (589,473,790):.\n- Positions (starting from the right, position 1 is ones):.\n1: 0.\n2:9.\n3:7.\n4:3.\n5:7.\n6:4.\n7:9.\n8:8.\n9:5.\n\nSecond number (219,574,375):.\nPositions:.\n1:5.\n2:7.\n3:3.\n4:4.\n5:7.\n6:5.\n7:9.\n8:1.\n9:2.\n\nNow, let's go step by step through each digit position:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 0 +5 =5. Write down 5. No carry.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):9 +7 =16. Write 6, carryover 1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):7 +3 =10 +1 (carry) =11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):3 +4 =7 +1 (carry) =8. Write 8, no carry.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):7 +7=14. Write 4, carryover1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):4 +5=9 +1 (carry)=10. Write 0, carryover1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):9 +9=18 +1 (carry)=19. Write 9, carryover1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):8 +1=9 +1 (carry)=10. Write 0, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):5 +2=7 +1 (carry)=8. Write 8, no carry.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from last to first (since we started from the right):.\n\nThe digits we wrote are, starting from position1 to 9:.\n\n5 (position1), 6 (position2),1 (3),8 (4),4 (5),0 (6),9 (7),0 (8),8 (9).\n\nWait, so the digits from right to left are:.\n\nPosition1:5.\n\nPosition2:6.\n\nPosition3:1.\n\nPosition4:8.\n\nPosition5:4.\n\nPosition6:0.\n\nPosition7:9.\n\nPosition8:0.\n\nPosition9:8.\n\nSo writing them in order from highest to lowest place (leftmost to rightmost):.\n\nStarting with the hundred millions place (position9):8,.\n\nthen ten millions (position8):0,.\n\nmillions (position7):9,.\n\nhundred thousands (position6):0,.\n\nten thousands (position5):4,.\n\nthousands (position4):8,.\n\nhundreds (position3):1,.\n\ntens (position2):6,.\n\nones (position1):5</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
