\nAdding them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2 +1 =3.\n\nTens:6 +7=13 → 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds:8 +1=9 plus 1 →10 →0, carryover1.\n\nThousands:5 +4=9 plus 1 →10 →0, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:7 (from first number\'s ten thousands place) +7 (from second number\'s ten thousands place) +1 (carryover) =15 →5, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:4 (from first) +2 (from second) +1 (carryover) =7 → no carryover.\n\nMillions:8 (first) +0 (second) =8.\n\nTen millions:7 (first) +2 (second) =9.\n\nHundred millions:3 +6=9.\n\nSo that gives 998,705,033. But the split method gave 998,750,033. There\'s a difference in the hundred thousands and ten thousands places?\n\nWait in the split method, the 475,862 +274,171 was 750,033. Let me check that again:\n\n475,862 + 274,171:\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\n475,862\n\n+274,171\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:2+1=3.\n\nTens:6+7=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:8+1=9 +1 →10 →0 carryover1.\n\nThousands:5 +4=9 +1 →10 →0 carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:7 (from first number\'s 475,862: the ten thousands place is 7?) Wait, 475,862 is the smaller part. Let\'s parse it:\n\n475,862 is 4 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 2 (ones).\n\nWait, 475,862: the digits are:\n\n4 (hundred thousands place),\n\n7 (ten thousands),\n\n5 (thousands),\n\n8 (hundreds),\n\n6 (tens),\n\n2 (ones).\n\nSimilarly, 274,171:\n\n2 (hundred thousands),\n\n7 (ten thousands),\n\n4 (thousands),\n\n1 (hundreds),\n\n7 (tens),\n\n1 (ones).\n\nSo adding the ten thousands place here:\n\n7 (from 475,862) +7 (from 274,171) =14, plus any carryover?\n\nWait, let\'s do the addition properly:\n\n475,862 + 274,171:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:2+1=3.\n\nTens:6+7=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:8+1=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nThousands:5 +4=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:7 +7=14 +1 (carryover) =15 →5, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:4 +2=6 +1 (carryover) =7.\n\nSo the result is 750,033. So the total sum would be 998,000,000 + 750,033 = 998,750,033.\n\nAh! So in the split method, the hundred thousands place in the small parts added to 7 (since 4+2+1=7), but in the column addition, the hundred thousands place was 4 (from first number) +2 (second) +1 (carryover) =7. That\'s consistent.\n\nWait, then why does the column addition give 998,705,033 instead of 998,750,033?\n\nWait, perhaps I miscounted the places in the column addition. Let me re-express the total sum from column addition:\n\nThe digits from right to left are:\n\nOnes:3\n\nTens:3\n\nHundreds:0\n\nThousands:0\n\nTen thousands:5 (from the 15 in ten thousands place)\n\nHundred thousands:7 (from 4+2+1)\n\nMillions:8 (from 8+0)\n\nTen millions:9 (7+2)\n\nHundreds millions:9 (3+6)\n\nSo combining these:\n\nHundreds millions:9\n\nTen millions:9\n\nMillions:8\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nTen thousands:5\n\nThousands:0\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:3\n\nOnes:3\n\nWait, so that would be 998,705,033. But the split method gave 998,750,033. The difference is in the ten thousands and hundred thousands places. In the column addition, the ten thousands is 5 and hundred thousands is7, leading to ...705... whereas the split method has ...750...\n\nAh! I think I see the confusion. The ten thousands place in the column addition is indeed 5, but in the split method, when adding the smaller parts, the ten thousands place in the smaller parts sum is 5, but that is in the context of the overall number.\n\nWait, let\'s write the column addition result step by step:\n\nStarting from the right, the digits are:\n\nPosition 1 (ones):3\n\n2 (tens):3\n\n3 (hundreds):0\n\n4 (thousands):0\n\n5 (ten thousands):5\n\n6 (hundred thousands):7\n\n7 (millions):8\n\n8 (ten millions):9\n\n9 (hundred millions):9\n\nSo the number is:\n\n9 (hundred millions),\n\n9 (ten millions),\n\n8 (millions),\n\n7 (hundred thousands),\n\n5 (ten thousands),\n\n0 (thousands),\n\n0 (hundreds),\n\n3 (tens),\n\n3 (ones).\n\nWhich is 998,705,033.\n\nBut in the split method, the total of the small 