 9 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nSo aligning them:.\n\n          3 6 0 6 4 0 0 5 6.\n        + 8 9 8 5 7 4 7 0 7.\n        ---------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 6 +7 =13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens:5 +0=5, plus the 1 carried over is 6. Write 6, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:0 +7=7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nThousands place:0 (from first number) +4 (from second)=4. Write 4, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:4 +7=11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:6 (from first number) +5 (second)=11, plus the carried 1 makes 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place:0 +8=8, plus carried 1 makes 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nTen millions place:6 +9=15. Write 5, carryover 1.\n\nHundred millions place:3 +8=11, plus the carried 1 makes 12. Write 2 and carryover 1. Since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes the next digit</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
