t is 9? Wait, no:\n\nWait 327,649,514:\n\nThe number is 327,649,514. Let\'s separate the digits with commas properly.\n\nIn the standard format, commas are placed every three digits from the right. So 327,649,514 is 327,649,514 → 327 (millions), 649 (thousands), 514. So:\n\n- Hundred millions: 3\n\n- Ten millions: 2\n\n- Millions:7\n\n- Hundred thousands:6\n\n- Ten thousands:4\n\n- Thousands:9\n\n- Hundreds:5\n\n- Tens:1\n\n- Units:4.\n\nYes, that\'s correct. So the thousands place is indeed 9.\n\nThe second number is 227,975,781:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n2 (hundred millions)\n\n2 (ten millions)\n\n7 (millions)\n\n9 (hundred thousands)\n\n7 (ten thousands)\n\n5 (thousands)\n\n7 (hundreds)\n\n8 (tens)\n\n1 (units).\n\nWait, let\'s confirm:\n\n227,975,781 → commas are after the first three digits from the right? Wait no, standard is commas every three digits. So 227,975,781 is 227,975,781 → 227 (millions), 975 (thousands), 781. So:\n\n- Hundred millions:2\n\n- Ten millions:2\n\n- Millions:7\n\n- Hundred thousands:9\n\n- Ten thousands:7\n\n- Thousands:5\n\n- Hundreds:7\n\n- Tens:8\n\n- Units:1.\n\nYes, so thousands place here is 5.\n\nTherefore, adding thousands place digits:9 (first number) +5 (second) =14 plus carryover 1 is 15. So 5 written, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nThen ten thousands place:4 (first) +7 (second) =11 +1 =12. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands place:6 +9 =15 +1=16. Correct.\n\nMillions place:7+7=14 +1=15. Correct.\n\nSo all steps are correct. So the sum should be 555,625,295. But the user\'s answer is 555,625,995. That\'s different in the hundreds and tens places?\n\nWait the user\'s answer has 995 at the end, but according to my calculation, the last digits are 295.\n\nWait let me check the hundreds place again. The hundreds digits:\n\nFirst number:5 (hundreds place)\n\nSecond number:7 (hundreds place). So 5 +7=12. So write 2, carryover1. That\'s correct. So hundreds digit is 2, not 9.\n\nWait the user\'s answer has 9 in the hundreds place? Wait 555,625,995: 