llions place in the final number is the 7th digit from the right. Let me see:\n\nThe final number as per my calculation is 1,751,081,712. The user\'s answer is 1,750,081,712. The difference is in the millions place: my result has a 1 there, but the user\'s answer has 0?\n\nWait, let me recalculate the millions place (position7):\n\nFirst number\'s millions digit: the first number is 981,574,076. Let\'s break down its digits:\n\n9 (hundred millions)\n\n8 (ten millions)\n\n1 (millions)\n\n5 (hundred thousands)\n\n7 (ten thousands)\n\n4 (thousands)\n\n0 (hundreds)\n\n7 (tens)\n\n6 (ones)\n\nSo the millions digit is indeed 1.\n\nSecond number: 769,507,636. Breaking down:\n\n7 (hundred millions)\n\n6 (ten millions)\n\n9 (millions)\n\n5 (hundred thousands)\n\n0 (ten thousands)\n\n7 (thousands)\n\n6 (hundreds)\n\n3 (tens)\n\n6 (ones)\n\nSo the millions digit is 9. So adding 1 +9 =10, plus the carryover from position6 (which was 1), so total 11. Therefore, 1 in that place, carryover1. That\'s correct. So the millions digit in the result is 1. So my calculation is correct, so the user\'s answer must be wrong? Or perhaps I made a mistake in another digit?\n\nWait let me check position5 (ten thousands place). First number\'s ten thousands digit is7, second\'s is0. Adding gives 7+0 + carryover (from position6\'s addition, which was 0, so no carryover there. Wait, position6 (hundred thousands) had a carryover of1 to position7. Wait, the carryover from position6 is to position7, so the addition at position5 (ten thousands) doesn\'t have any carryover. So 7+0=7, plus any carryover? Wait position5\'s addition is after position6? Wait no, positions are from right to left, so the carryover propagates to the next higher digit. Let me check:\n\nPosition1 (ones): sum 12 → carry1.\n\nPosition2 (tens): sum 11 → carry1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds): sum7 → no carry.\n\nPosition4 (thousands): sum11 → carry1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands): sum7 +1 (carry from position4) → 8, no carry.\n\nPosition6