      "text": "1,519,284,76? Wait, let me form the number correctly.\n\nWait let me write each digit in order:\n\nBillions place: 1,\n\nHundred millions:5,\n\nTen millions:1,\n\nMillions:9,\n\nHundred thousands:9,\n\nTen thousands:2,\n\nThousands:8,\n\nHundreds:4,\n\nTens:7,\n\nOnes:6.\n\nSo combining these digits:\n\n1 (billion), 5 (hundred million), 1 (ten million), 9 (million), 9 (hundred thousand), 2 (ten thousand), 8 (thousand), 4 (hundred), 7 (ten), 6 (one).\n\nSo written out: 1,519,284,76? Wait, no, let's see:\n\nBreaking into groups:\n\nBillions digit:1,\n\nThen hundred millions:5,\n\nTen millions:1,\n\nMillions:9,\n\nThen comma, then hundred thousands:9,\n\nTen thousands:2,\n\nThousands:8,\n\nThen comma, hundreds:4,\n\nTens:7,\n\nOnes:6.\n\nSo the number is 1,519,284,76? Wait that can't be right. Wait, let's count the digits:\n\n1 (1), 5 (2),1 (3),9 (4),9 (5),2 (6),8 (7),4 (8),7 (9),6 (10). So it's a 10-digit number starting with 1 followed by 5,1,9, etc.\n\nSo the number is 1,519,284,766? Wait, let me reconstruct:\n\nDigits from highest to lowest (billions down to ones):\n\n1 (billions),\n\n5 (hundred millions),\n\n1 (ten millions),\n\n9 (millions),\n\n9 (hundred thousands),\n\n2 (ten thousands),\n\n8 (thousands),\n\n4 (hundreds),\n\n7 (tens),\n\n6 (ones).\n\nSo writing as: 1,519,928,476? Wait no. Wait, let's structure properly:\n\nThe first three digits after the billions would be the hundred millions, ten millions, millions: 5,1,9.\n\nThen the next three (hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands):9,2,8.\n\nThen the last three (hundreds, tens, ones):4,7,6.\n\nSo the full number is 1,519,928,476? Wait, but commas are placed every three digits from the right.\n\nWait let me do it step by step:\n\nThe digits are: 1 (billions place),\n\nthen 5 (hundred millions),\n\n1 (ten millions),\n\n9 (millions),\n\nso the first four digits (billions and below) are 1 5 1 9,\n\nthen next three digits (hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands): 9,2,8,\n\nthen the last