h digit from the right, which is 8.\n\nSo adding millions place:2 +8 =10. So that's 0 with a carryover of 1. Wait, but in my initial calculation I had 8+8. Hmm, that's where the mistake was earlier. Oh no! I must have messed up the millions place.\n\nWait, so let's start over the reasoning properly, step by step.\n\nLet me list all digits with their places:.\n\nFirst number (882,092,648):.\n\nPosition (from right):.\n\n1:8 (ones).\n\n2:4 (tens).\n\n3:6 (hundreds).\n\n4:2 (thousands).\n\n5:9 (ten thousands).\n\n6:0 (hundred thousands).\n\n7:2 (millions).\n\n8:8 (ten millions).\n\n9:8 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number (648,639,351):.\n\n1:1 (ones).\n\n2:5 (tens).\n\n3:3 (hundreds).\n\n4:9 (thousands).\n\n5:3 (ten thousands).\n\n6:6 (hundred thousands).\n\n7:8 (millions).\n\n8:4 (ten millions).\n\n9:6 (hundred millions).\n\nNow adding each column from right to left, keeping track of carries:.\n\nStarting with Position1 (ones):.\n\n8 +1 =9. No carryover. Result:9.\n\nPosition2 (tens):.\n\n4 +5 =9. Result:9.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):.\n\n6 +3 =9. Result:9.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):.\n\n2 +9 =11. Write 1, carryover1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):.\n\n9 +3 =12 +1 (carry) =13. Write 3, carryover1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):.\n\n0 +6 =6 +1 (carry) =7. Write7, no carryover.\n\nPosition7 (millions):.\n\n2 +8 =10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):.\n\n8 +4 =12 +1 (carry) =13. Write3, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):.\n\n8 +6 =14 +1 (carry) =15. Write5, carryover1.\n\nNow, since we've reached the highest digit (hundred millions), but there's still a carryover of 1. So we need to add a new digit to the left: billions place.\n\nBillions place: 1 (carryover). So the total digits now have an extra digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting all together from left to right:.\n\nBillions:1,.\n\nHundred millions:5,.\n\nTen millions:3,.\n\nMillions:0,.\n\nHundred thousands:7,.\n\nTen thousands:3,.\n\nThousands:1,.\n\nHundreds:9,.\n\nTens:9,.\n\nOnes:9.\n\nWait