 that down.\n\nWait a second, let me check again. Maybe I missed a digit. Let me count the digits in each number. .\n\nFirst number: 207,512,855. That's 9 digits. Breaking down: 2 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 322,924,497. Also 9 digits. 3 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nSo when adding, let me list each place step by step:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 5 +7 =12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nTens:5+9=14 +1=15. Write 5, carry1.\n\nHundreds:8+4=12 +1=13. Write3, carry1.\n\nThousands:2+4=6 +1=7. Write7, no carry.\n\nTen thousands:1+2=3. Write3.\n\nHundred thousands:5+9=14. Write4, carry1.\n\nMillions:7+2=9 +1=10. Write0, carry1.\n\nTen millions:0+2=2 +1=3. Wait, hold on. Wait the first number's ten millions place is 0, and the second is 2? Wait let's see:.\n\nWait the first number is 207,512,855. So breaking down:.\n\nHundred millions:2.\n\nTen millions:0.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nHundred thousands:5.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nThousands:2.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nTens:5.\n\nOnes:5.\n\nSecond number: 322,924,497:.\n\nHundred millions:3.\n\nTen millions:2.\n\nMillions:2.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:2.\n\nThousands:4.\n\nHundreds:4.\n\nTens:9.\n\nOnes:7.\n\nSo Ten millions place for first is 0, second is 2. So adding 0+2 =2, plus any carryover? Wait when we were at millions place, after adding 7 (from first number's millions) and 2 (second's millions) plus the carryover from hundred thousands (which was 1) gave 10. So that carryover to the ten millions place is 1. .\n\nWait let me redo the steps carefully.\n\nStarting over step by step:.\n\nAlign the numbers:.\n\n       2 0 7 5 1 2 8 5 5.\n\n     + 3 2 2 9 2 4 4 9 7.\n\n     -----------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes:5 +7 =12. Write down 2, carryover 1.\n\nTens:5 +9 =14, plus 1 →15. Write 5, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:8 +4 =12, plus1 →13. Write3, carryover1.\n\nThousands:2 +4 =6, plus1 →7. Write7, no carry.\n\nTen thousands:1 +2 =3. Write3.\n\nHundred thousands:5 +9 =14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nMillions:7 (first) +2 (second) =9, plus carryover1 →10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:0 (first) +2 (second) =2, plus carryover1 →3. Write3.\n\nHundred millions:2 +3 =5. Write5.\n\nWait wait, that can't be. Wait the hundred millions place: first number has 2, second has 3. So 2+3=5. But in the ten millions place, first number has 0 and second has 2, plus the carryover 1 from millions, so 0+2+1=3. .\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum would be:.\n\nStarting from the right, digits are:.\n\nOnes:2.\n\nTens:5.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:3.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nMillions:0.\n\nTen millions:3.\n\nHundred millions:5.\n\nWait that would give the number 530,343,732? Wait let me write the digits in order:.\n\nHundred millions:5.\n\nTen millions:3.\n\nMillions:0.\n\nHundred thousands:3?.\n\nWait I think I messed up the place values. Let me list each digit position step by step.\n\nLet me structure it properly:.\n\nEach digit from right to left (ones to hundred millions):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 5 +7 =12 → 2, carry1.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):5 +9 +1 =15 →5, carry1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):8 +4 +1 =13 →3, carry1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):2 +4 +0 =6 + carry1 →7, carry0.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):1 +2 =3 →3, carry0.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5 +9 =14 →4, carry1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):7 +2 +1 (carry) =10 →0, carry1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):0 +2 +1 (carry) =3 →3, carry0.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):2 +3 =5 →5, carry0.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:.\n\n2 (ones),5 (tens),3 (hundreds),7 (thousands),3 (ten thousands),4 (hundred thousands),0 (millions),3 (ten millions),5 (hundred millions).\n\nSo writing the number from highest to lowest place:.\n\nHundred millions (5), ten millions (3), mi