ns:9 +5=14 → 4, carryover 1.\n\n3. Hundreds:4 +0 +1=5 →5.\n\n4. Thousands:8 +3=11 →1, carryover1.\n\n5. Ten thousands:7 +1 +1=9 →9.\n\n6. Hundred thousands:3 +3=6 →6.\n\n7. Millions:5 +2=7 →7.\n\n8. Ten millions:6 +2=8 →8.\n\n9. Hundred millions:4 +2=6 →6.\n\nSo combining all the digits from right to left (since we started from ones, the first digit is the ones, then tens, etc.), the sum would be:.\n\n6 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions),7 (millions),6 (hundred thousands),9 (ten thousands),1 (thousands),5 (hundreds),4 (tens),9 (ones).\n\nWait, actually, when we write the number, the order is from highest to lowest place. So the digits are:.\n\nHundred millions:6,.\n\nTen millions:8,.\n\nMillions:7,.\n\nHundred thousands:6,.\n\nTen thousands:9,.\n\nThousands:1,.\n\nHundreds:5,.\n\nTens:4,.\n\nOnes:9</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
