final_output:  ['1,406,712,094? Wait, but the user\'s thought says the correct answer is 1,406,712,074. Hmm, there\'s a discrepancy here. I must have made a mistake in my calculation.\n\nLet me check again step by step. Maybe I miscalculated one of the digits.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically aligned:\n\n          6 0 7 0 6 9 4 6 4\n        + 7 9 9 6 4 2 6 3 0\n        --------------------\n\nLet me write each digit position:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nPosition 1 (Ones): 4 + 0 = 4.\n\nPosition 2 (Tens): 6 + 3 = 9.\n\nPosition 3 (Hundreds): 4 + 6 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 4 (Thousands): 9 + 2 = 11 + 1 (carryover) = 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 5 (Ten thousands): 6 + 4 =10 +1 =11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 6 (Hundred thousands): 0 +6 =6 +1 =7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nPosition 7 (Millions):7 +9 =16. Write 6, carryover1.\n\nPosition 8 (Ten millions):0 +9 =9 +1 =10. Write 0, carryover1.\n\nPosition 9 (Hundred millions):6 +7 =13 +1 =14. Write 4, carryover1.\n\nPosition 10 (Billions): 0 +0 +1 =1.\n\nSo the digits from right to left (positions 1 to 10):\n\nPosition 1:4\n\n2:9\n\n3:0\n\n4:2\n\n5:1\n\n6:7\n\n7:6\n\n8:0\n\n9:4\n\n10:1\n\nWait, but arranging them in order, the digits are:\n\nBillions (position10):1\n\nHundred millions (position9):4\n\nTen millions (position8):0\n\nMillions (position7):6\n\nHundred thousands (position6):7\n\nTen thousands (position5):1\n\nThousands (position4):2\n\nHundreds (position3):0\n\nTens (position2):9\n\nOnes (position1):4\n\nSo the number is 1,406,712,094.\n\nBut the user\'s thought says 1,406,712,074. Hmm, so there\'s a difference in the thousands place maybe? Let me check again the thousands place calculation.\n\nPosition4 (Thousands place):\n\nFirst number\'s thousands digit: looking at 607,069,464. Breaking down:\n\n607,069,464:\n\nLet\'s parse each digit:\n\nDigit positions (from right):\n\n1 (ones):4\n\n2 (tens):6\n\n3 (hundreds):4\n\n4 (thousands):9\n\nWait, 607,069,464: the