digits here are 1 (from the first number) and 6 (from the second). 1 + 6 = 7. So 7 in ten-millions.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:** Finally, the highest digits here: 2 and 5. 2 + 5 = 7. So that's 7 in the hundred-millions place</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
