      "text": "1,024,994,569? Wait, but the user said they think the correct answer is 1,024,994,566. Hmm, so there's a discrepancy here. Did I make a mistake?\n\nWait, let me recalculate step by step again to check where the error is.\n\nLet me re-add each digit carefully:\n\nFirst, let me write both numbers vertically:\n\n      464,101,179\n    +560,893,390\n    --------------\n\nAdding digit by digit from right to left.\n\nOnes place: 9 +0 =9. Correct.\n\nTens place:7+9=16. Write 6, carryover1.\n\nHundreds place:1 (from first number) +3 (second number) +1 (carryover)=5. Correct.\n\nThousands place:1 (first) +3 (second)=4. Correct.\n\nTen thousands place:0 (first) +9 (second)=9. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands place:1 (first) +8 (second)=9. Correct.\n\nMillions place:4 (first) +0 (second)=4. Correct.\n\nTen millions place:6 (first) +6 (second)=12. Write 2, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions place:4 (first) +5 (second)=9, plus the 1 carried over makes 10. So write 0 and carryover1 to the next (billions) place.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred millions:0.\n\nTen millions:2.\n\nMillions:4.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:9.\n\nThousands:4.\n\nHundreds:5.\n\nTens:6.\n\nOnes:9.\n\nSo combining: 1,024,994,569.\n\nBut the user's answer is 1,024,994,566. Hmm, so where's the mistake?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up a digit in one of the numbers. Let me check the original numbers again.\n\nThe first number is 464,101,179. Let's confirm each digit:\n\n4 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions),4 (millions),1 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),1 (thousands),1 (hundreds),7 (tens),9 (ones). That's correct.\n\nSecond number is 560,893,390. Breaking down:\n\n5 (hundred millions),6 (ten millions),0 (millions),8 (hundred thousands),9 (ten thousands),3 (thousands),3 (hundreds),9 (tens),0 (ones). Yes.\n\nWait, in the hundreds place of the second number, it's 3, not 3? Wait, let me check the second number again:\n\n560,893,390.\n\nBreaking into digits:\n\nDigits from left