n\nPosition 6 (Hundred thousands): 6 + 2 = 8 → 8.\n\nPosition 7 (Millions): 1 + 6 = 7 → 7.\n\nPosition 8 (Ten millions): 2 + 2 = 4 →4.\n\nPosition 9 (Hundred millions): 6 + 1 = 7 →7.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left:.\n\nPositions 1 to 9:.\n\nDigits: 6 (position1), 7 (2), 0 (3), 4 (4), 1 (5), 8 (6), 7 (7), 4 (8), 7 (9).\n\nSo the number would be 7 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 6 (ones). Wait, let me arrange them properly:.\n\nThe digits from highest to lowest place:.\n\nHundred millions: 7.\n\nTen millions:4.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nHundred thousands:8.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nThousands:4.\n\nHundreds:0.\n\nTens:7.\n\nOnes:6</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
