ach.\n\nAlternatively, let me add the two numbers:\n\nFirst number: 940,833,598\n\nSecond number:885,048,752\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet\'s add 940,833,598 + 800,000,000 = 1,740,833,598.\n\nThen add the remaining 85,048,752:\n\n1,740,833,598 +85,048,752 = ?\n\nAdding 1,740,833,598 +80,000,000 = 1,820,833,598.\n\nThen add 5,048,752:\n\n1,820,833,598 +5,000,000 =1,825,833,598.\n\nThen add 48,752: 1,825,833,598 +48,752 =1,825,882,350. Exactly matches.\n\nSo the correct answer is indeed 1,825,882,350. The user\'s answer of 1,425,882,350 is off by 400 million, likely due to an error in their addition steps.\n\nTherefore, the final computed sum is 1,825,882,350.\n</think>', ''] 38%|###7      | 189/500 [7:27:25<11:00:44, 127.47s/it]
