tions again. Wait, maybe I miscounted the places. Let me recount to be sure.\n\nWait, 877,001,467 is 9 digits: 8 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nThe second number is 418,246,764. That's also 9 digits: 4 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 4 (ones). Wait, so when adding, the billions place would be the 10th digit, but since both are 9 digits, their highest is hundred millions. So adding the hundred millions: 8 +4 =12. So that gives 2 in the hundred millions and carryover 1 to the billions place. Since there's no more digits, that 1 becomes a 1 in the billions place</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
