\nSo putting all the digits together from the positions:.\n\nStarting from the highest, we have the carried 1, then the result of position8 (7), position7 (4), position6 (3), position5 (7), position4 (1), position3 (2), position2 (2), position1 (7), position0 (0).\n\nWait let me list them in order:.\n\nThe positions from 0 to 8 give the digits from right to left. The total result will be:.\n\nCarryover1 (from position8's addition), then the digit from position8 (7), then position7 (4), position6 (3), position5 (7), position4 (1), position3 (2), position2 (2), position1 (7), position0 (0). Wait, no, the digits are written from the carryover first, then the position8, then down.\n\nWait actually, the carryover from position8 is 1, so the digits are:.\n\n1 (from carryover), then the digit from position8 (7), then position7 (4), position6 (3), position5 (7), position4 (1), position3 (2), position2 (2), position1 (7), position0 (0).\n\nWait, but the order should be:.\n\nThe first digit (leftmost) is the carryover 1, followed by the digits starting from the highest position (position8):.\n\nSo total digits are:.\n\n1 (carryover),.\n\nposition8:7,.\n\nposition7:4,.\n\nposition6:3,.\n\nposition5:7,.\n\nposition4:1,.\n\nposition3:2,.\n\nposition2:2,.\n\nposition1:7,.\n\nposition0:0</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
