arryover1 to ten thousands.\n\nSo the total after thousands is 1,544,140,000 +16,000 \u21921,544,156,000. Which matches the digit-by-digit's ten thousands digit (5) and the thousands digit (6). Because the ten thousands digit is5 (from 15 in step5), which includes the carryover from thousands place.\n\nWait, but in the digit-by-digit result, the ten thousands digit is5 (from step5), which is 50,000. But in the calculator approach, the ten thousands place is140,000. The difference is because in digit-by-digit, the carryover from thousands (1) is added to the ten thousands' sum (14 \u219215). So 15 in ten thousands place gives 5, and carryover1 to the hundred thousands. So the ten thousands digit is5 (50,000), but the total contribution from ten thousands place plus carryover is 15 (ten thousands) plus carryover to hundred thousands. So overall, the total is correctly accounted for.\n\nTherefore, the digit-by-digit result of1,544,152,604 is correct. But the calculator method I did earlier must have had an error. Wait in the step-by-step calculator method I added 689,268,179 +854,884,265 as follows:\n\nFirst adding 600M+800M=1400M,\n\nthen 80M+50M=130M \u2192 total1530M,\n\nthen 9M+4M=13M \u21921543M,\n\nthen 200k+800k=1M \u2192 total1544M,\n\nthen 60k+80k=140k \u21921544,140k,\n\n8k+8k=16k \u21921544,156k,\n\n100+400=500 \u21921544,156,500,\n\n70+20=90 \u21921544,156,590,\n\n9+5=14 \u2192 total1544,156,604.\n\nBut this contradicts the digit-by-digit result. The error must be in the calculator method's breakdown.\n\nWait the hundred thousands place addition:200k+800k=1,000,000 \u2192 which is 1 million. This is added to the previous total of1,543M (from hundreds of millions, ten millions, millions). So 1,543M +1M =1,544M. But the millions place in the digit-by-digit was 14M (from 13M +1M carryover?), but how?\n\nWait, the millions place in the first number is9M, second is4M \u21929+4=13M. Plus the carryover1 from hundred thousands (which was 1M), totaling14M. So the mi