dreds digit is 0.\n\nSo position 3 (hundreds): 0 + 2 (from second number\'s hundreds digit which is 2) → 0+2=2. So that\'s correct.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):.\n\nFirst number\'s thousands digit: the fourth digit from right. The number is 328,739,002. The thousands place is the fourth digit: looking at 002 (ones, tens, hundreds), then the thousands is the next one, which is 9? Wait, maybe I need to re-express the number properly.\n\nWait, perhaps breaking it down with commas is easier. The first number is 328,739,002. The commas are placed every three digits starting from the right. So:.\n\n328,739,002 → 328 (million), 739 (thousand), 002. So the thousands digit would be the first digit of the "thousands" part, which is 7 (from 739,002). Wait, actually, maybe I\'m getting confused here.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps writing out each digit\'s place:.\n\nLet me write both numbers digit by digit, starting from the right (ones place):.\n\nFirst number: 328,739,002.\n\nDigits (from right to left):.\n\n1: 2 (ones).\n\n2: 0 (tens).\n\n3: 0 (hundreds).\n\n4: 9 (thousands).\n\n5: 3 (ten thousands).\n\n6: 7 (hundred thousands).\n\n7: 8 (millions).\n\n8: 2 (ten millions).\n\n9: 3 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 386,190,257.\n\nDigits (from right to left):.\n\n1:7 (ones).\n\n2:5 (tens).\n\n3:2 (hundreds).\n\n4:0 (thousands).\n\n5:9 (ten thousands).\n\n6:1 (hundred thousands).\n\n7:6 (millions).\n\n8:8 (ten millions).\n\n9:3 (hundred millions).\n\nSo now, adding each column:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 2 +7=9 → write 9.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):0+5=5 →5.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):0+2=2 →2.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):9 (from first) +0 (from second)=9 →9.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):3 +9=12 → write 2, carryover 1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):7 +1=8, plus the carryover 1 →9. So 8+1? Wait, 7 (first) +1 (second)=8, plus 1 carried over →9. So write 9, no carryover.\n\nWait, let me recast:.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):.\n\nFirst number\'s digit:7.\n\nSecond number\'s digit:1 (from second number\'s hundred thousands place).\n\nSo 7 +1 =8, plus any carryover from previous position (position5 had a carryover of 1? Wait position5 was ten thousands place.\n\nWait position5 (ten thousands): first number has 3, second has 9 → 3+9=12. So write 2, carryover 1 to the next (hundred thousands place). .\n\nSo in position6 (hundred thousands):.\n\n7 (first) +1 (second) +1 (carryover) =9. So no carryover here.\n\nPosition7 (millions):.\n\nFirst number\'s digit:8.\n\nSecond\'s digit:6 →8+6=14. So write 4, carryover 1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):.\n\nFirst\'s digit:2 + second\'s 8 =10, plus carryover 1 →11. So write 1, carryover 1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):.\n\nFirst\'s digit:3 + second\'s 3 =6, plus carryover 1 →7.\n\nSo putting all together from right to left:.\n\nPositions:.\n\n1:9.\n\n2:5.\n\n3:2.\n\n4:9.\n\n5:2 (with a carried 1 to next).\n\n6:9.\n\n7:4 (with carried 1 from here to next).\n\n8:1 (with carried 1).\n\n9:7.\n\nWait, let me list all the digits from the positions:.\n\nStarting from position1 (ones) up to position9 (hundred millions):.\n\nPosition1:9.\n\nPosition2:5.\n\nPosition3:2.\n\nPosition4:9.\n\nPosition5:2 (since ten thousands place had 12, so 2 written).\n\nPosition6:9 (from 7+1+1?).\n\nWait let me go step by step again.\n\nLet me re-calculate each column carefully:.\n\n1. Ones place: 2 +7=9. Write 9. Carryover 0.\n\n2. Tens:0+5=5. Write5. Carryover0.\n\n3. Hundreds:0+2=2. Write2. Carryover0.\n\n4. Thousands:9+0=9. Write9. Carryover0.\n\n5. Ten thousands:3+9=12. Write2. Carryover1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands:7+1=8, plus carryover1 →9. Write9. Carryover0.\n\n7. Millions:8+6=14. Write4. Carryover1.\n\n8. Ten millions:2+8=10, plus carryover1 →11. Write1. Carryover1.\n\n9. Hundred millions:3+3=6, plus carryover1 →7. Write7. No more digits.\n\nSo the digits from position1 to position9 (right to left) are:.\n\n9 (ones),5,2,9,2,9,4,1,7.\n\nSo writing the number from left to right (hundred millions to ones):.\n\n7 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),2 (hundreds),5 (tens),9 (ones).\n\nWait, wait, that can\'t be. Wait, the digits are in the order of positions 9 down to 1, so the final number is:.\n\nPosition9:7 (hundred millions place).\n\nPosition8:1 (ten millions).\n\nPosition7:4 (millions).\n\nPosition6:9 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition5:2 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition4:9 (thousands).\n\nPosition3:2 (hundreds).\n\nPosition2:5 (tens).\n\nPosition1:9 (ones).\n\nSo combining them:.\n\n7 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 9 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is ']]
