Let\'s write each digit\'s place properly.\n\nLet me write both numbers digit by digit from right to left (since addition starts from the right):\n\nFirst number (937243152):\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 2\n\nPosition 2 (tens):5\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1\n\nPosition4 (thousands):3\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):4\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):2\n\nPosition7 (millions):7\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):3\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):9\n\nSecond number (439376158):\n\nPosition1 (ones):8\n\nPosition2 (tens):5\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1\n\nPosition4 (thousands):6\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):7\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):3\n\nPosition7 (millions):9\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):3\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):4\n\nWait a second! The thousands place for the second number is 6, not 1. Wait, let me check the second number again: 439,376,158.\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n4 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nAh! There\'s the mistake. Earlier, in the thousands place, I thought the second number had a 1, but actually, the thousands digit is 6. Let me recalculate with that.\n\nLet me redo the addition properly step by step:\n\nStarting over:\n\nPositions (from right to left):\n\n1. Ones: 2 +8=10 → 0, carry 1\n2. Tens:5 +5=10 +1=11 →1, carry1\n3. Hundreds:1 +1=2 +1=3? Wait wait. Wait the hundreds place for first number is 1, second number\'s hundreds digit is 1 (from the breakdown of 439,376,158: the hundreds place is 1). So 1+1=2 plus carryover 1 is 3? Wait no, the second number\'s hundreds digit is 1. So 1+1=2 plus 1 carried over is 3. So hundreds digit is 3, carryover 0.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought it was 8. Hmm, confusion here. Let me do each step carefully.\n\nWait let me list each digit\'s place for both numbers properly:\n\nFirst number: 937,243,152\n\nDigits from right (position 1 to 9):\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 2\n\nPosition 2 (tens):5\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1\n\nPosi