nd digit from the left, which is 3).\n\nSecond number\'s ten millions digit is 3 (from 439,376,158 → the second digit from the left is 3).\n\nPlus the carryover from millions place addition (which was 1 from 16). So 3 +3 +1 =7. That\'s correct. So the ten millions digit is 7. So the hundred millions digit is 9+4=13, so 3 with carryover to billions.\n\nWait then where does the 8 in the user\'s answer come from? The user\'s answer is 1,378,619,310. So in the hundred millions place it\'s 3, ten millions is 7, millions is 6, but the ten thousands is 1, so the number is 1,3 (hundred millions),7 (ten millions),6 (millions),6 (hundred thousands),1 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),3 (hundreds),1 (tens),0 (ones). So 1,376,619,310.\n\nThe user\'s answer is 1,378,619,310. The difference is in the millions place? Wait no, in the millions place I have 6, user has 6. Ten millions is 7, so the number is 1,376... versus user\'s 1,378... So the discrepancy is in the hundred millions and ten millions? Wait no, the first three digits are 1,3,7. The user\'s is 1,3,7, so that\'s same. The next is 8? Wait maybe I messed up the hundred thousands place?\n\nWait let\'s check again step by step:\n\nLet me list all digits again properly:\n\nStarting from the right (positions 1 to 9):\n\nPosition 1 (Ones): 2 + 8 =10 → 0, carry 1\n\nPosition 2 (Tens):5 +5 =10 +1=11 →1, carry 1\n\nPosition3 (Hundreds):1 +1 =2 +1=3 →3, carry 0\n\nPosition4 (Thousands):3 +6 =9 →9, carry 0\n\nPosition5 (Ten thousands):4 +7=11 →1, carry1\n\nPosition6 (Hundred thousands):2 +3=5 +1=6 →6, carry0\n\nPosition7 (Millions):7 +9=16 →6, carry1\n\nPosition8 (Ten millions):3 +3=6 +1=7 →7, carry0\n\nPosition9 (Hundred millions):9 +4=13 →3, carry1\n\nThen the final carry1 → billions place 1.\n\nSo the result is 1,376,619,310.\n\nWait the user\'s answer is 1,378,619,310. So the difference is in the ten millions place? Wait no, the ten millions digit is 7 in my calculation. The user\'s answer has 8 in the millions place? Let me see:\