7,358,704 and 447,557,173. Let me count the digits again to ensure alignment. .\n\nFirst number: 6 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 7 (millions), etc. The second number is 4 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 7 (millions). So when adding the hundred millions place: 6 (from first number) plus 4 (from second number) plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. So that would be 1 in the hundred millions and carry over 1 to the billions place. .\n\nSo the total sum would have a 1 in the billions place, 1 in the hundred millions, then the rest as calculated. Let me reconstruct all the digits step by step:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 7.\n\nTens:7.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nThousands:5 (with a carryover 1).\n\nTen thousands:1 (with carryover 1).\n\nHundred thousands:1 (with carryover 1).\n\nMillions:2 (with carryover 1).\n\nTen millions:2 (with carryover 1).\n\nHundred millions:1 (with carryover 1).\n\nBillions:1 (since we carried over 1 here)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
