Position 3 (hundreds):5.\nPosition 4 (thousands):4.\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):5.\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):9.\nPosition 7 (millions):9.\nPosition 8 (ten millions):3.\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):9.\n\nSecond number:155,977,622.\nDigits from right (ones) to left (hundred millions):.\nPosition 1 (ones):2.\nPosition 2 (tens):2.\nPosition 3 (hundreds):6.\nPosition 4 (thousands):7.\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):7.\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):9.\nPosition 7 (millions):5.\nPosition 8 (ten millions):5.\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):1.\n\nWait, but when adding, the alignment is such that each corresponding place is added. So, let me make sure each digit is correctly aligned. Let's write them vertically with all digits:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\nOnes place:.\n4 (from first number) + 2 (from second number) = 6. So 6 in ones.\n\nTens place:.\n3 + 2 = 5. So 5 in tens.\n\nHundreds place:.\n5 + 6 = 11. So write 1, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:.\n4 + 7 = 11, plus the carryover 1 makes 12. So 2 here, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place:.\n5 (from first number) +7 (from second) + 1 (carryover) = 13. So write 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n9 +9 =18, plus 1 =19. Write 9, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place:.\n9 (first) +5 (second) +1=15. Write 5, carryover 1.\n\nTen millions place:.\n3 +5 =8 plus 1=9. No carryover here.\n\nHundred millions place:.\n9 +1 =10. So write 0 and carryover 1. Wait, but since that's the highest place, do we need an extra digit? So the total would be 1,0 followed by the rest?.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again carefully:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1. Ones place: 4 +2 =6. Write 6.\n\n2. Tens:3+2=5. Write 5.\n\n3. Hundreds:5+6=11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\n4. Thousands:4+7=11 +1=12. Write 2, carryover1.\n\n5. Ten thousands:5 +7=12 +1 (carryover) =13. Wait, hold on, the first number's ten thousands place is 5 (since the number is 939,954,534. Breaking down: 939 million, 954 thousand, 534. So the digi