itions:\n\nFirst number digits (from position0 to 8):\n\nPosition0:9,\n\n1:9,\n\n2:2,\n\n3:1,\n\n4:2,\n\n5:5,\n\n6:8,\n\n7:4,\n\n8:7.\n\nSecond number digits (positions0-8):\n\nPosition0:9,\n\n1:2,\n\n2:5,\n\n3:4,\n\n4:2,\n\n5:0,\n\n6:7,\n\n7:3,\n\n8:9.\n\nNow adding each position:\n\nPosition0 (units):\n\n9+9=18 →8, carry1.\n\nPosition1 (tens):\n\n9+2=11 +1=12 →2, carry1.\n\nPosition2 (hundreds):\n\n2+5=7 +1=8 →8, carry0.\n\nPosition3 (thousands):\n\n1+4=5 →5, carry0.\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):\n\n2+2=4 →4.\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands):\n\n5+0=5 →5.\n\nPosition6 (millions):\n\n8+7=15 →5, carry1.\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):\n\n4+3=7 +1=8 →8, carry0.\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):\n\n7+9=16 →6, carry1.\n\nPosition9 (billions):\n\ncarry1 →1.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nPosition9:1,\n\n8:6,\n\n7:8,\n\n6:5,\n\n5:5,\n\n4:4,\n\n3:5,\n\n2:8,\n\n1:2,\n\n0:8.\n\nThus the number is1,685,548,828.\n\nBut breakdown gives1,685,545,828. The difference is3,000. Where is this?\n\nWait the breakdown method\'s total is1,685,545,828.\n\nDigit-wise\'s total is1,685,548,828.\n\nThe difference is in the thousands place: digit-wise has5 in thousands place (position3), breakdown\'s thousands is5 as well. So the difference must be in another digit.\n\nWait let me check position6 (millions):\n\nDigit-wise has5 in millions place (position6).\n\nBreakdown\'s millions digit is5 (from the original 748 million\'s millions digit plus the second number\'s millions digit? Wait no, the breakdown\'s millions digit comes from the 1,685,000,000 which has5 in millions place (since 748 +937 =1685 million → 1,685,000,000). So the millions digit is5. The digit-wise also has5 there. So that matches.\n\nWait the difference must be in the hundred thousands place. Wait digit-wise has5 in hundred thousands (position5). Breakdown\'s hundred thousands is5 (from breakdown\'s addition). So that\'s same.\n\nWait let me check the ten thousands place (position4): both have4.\n\nHmm, where is the 3,000 difference?