m step by step:\n\nFirst number: 749,607,278\n\nSecond number:426,850,538\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes digit: 8 +8 =16. 6, carryover1.\n\nTens:7+3=10, plus 1=11. 1, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:2+5=7 plus 1=8, no carryover.\n\nThousands:7+0=7.\n\nTen thousands:0+5=5.\n\nHundred thousands:6+8=14 →4, carryover1.\n\nMillions:9+6=15, plus 1 (carryover)=16 →6, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:4+2=6, plus 1=7.\n\nHundred millions:7+4=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there\'s a carryover from the hundred millions (11), we add the 1 to the billions place, making it 1.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nTen millions:7\n\nMillions:6\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:5\n\nThousands:7\n\nHundreds:8\n\nTens:1\n\nOnes:6\n\nThus the total is 1,176,457,816.\n\nBut the user\'s answer was 2,176,457,816. So there\'s a discrepancy here. Maybe I made an error in a digit?\n\nWait, let me try adding the numbers in another way. Let\'s convert them to numbers and add.\n\nFirst number: 749,607,278.\n\nSecond number:426,850,538.\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me add the numbers:\n\n749,607,278\n\n+426,850,538\n\nStart adding:\n\nUnits place: 8+8=16 → 6, carryover 1.\n\nTens:7+3+1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:2+5+1=8.\n\nThousands:7+0=7.\n\nTen thousands:0+5=5.\n\nHundred thousands:6+8=14 →4, carryover1.\n\nMillions:9+6+1=16 →6, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:4+2+1=7.\n\nHundred millions:7+4=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nThen the carryover 1 becomes the billions place: 1.\n\nSo the total is 1,176,457,816. But the user\'s answer is 2,176,457,816, which is 1,000,000,000 more. That suggests that maybe I miscalculated the hundred millions place?\n\nWait, let me check the hundred millions digits again:\n\nFirst number\'s hundred millions digit is 7 (since 749,607,278 is 7 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 9 (millions)... yes, the first digit is 7 in the hundred millions place.\n\nSecond number is 426,850,538 → the first digit is 4 (hundred millions place).\