      "text": "1,150,919,431. Wait, but the user said they think the correct answer is 1,150,919,461. Hmm, there's a discrepancy here. Let me check my calculations again because the user's answer might be correct, or maybe I made a mistake.\n\nLooking at the thousands place again: first number's thousands digit is 6, second is 2. 6+2 is 8 plus no carryover (since the hundreds place carried over 1, but after that, the thousands place was 6+2=8 plus 0? Wait, let me check step by step again.\n\nWait, let's redo the addition step by step with each digit:\n\nLet me write both numbers with commas for clarity:\n\nFirst number: 485,926,471 \u2192 breaking down each digit from right to left:\n\nOnes:1\n\nTens:7\n\nHundreds:4\n\nThousands:6\n\nTen thousands:2\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nMillions:5\n\nTen millions:8\n\nHundred millions:4\n\nSecond number:664,992,960 \u2192 digits:\n\nOnes:0\n\nTens:6\n\nHundreds:9\n\nThousands:2\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nMillions:4\n\nTen millions:6\n\nHundred millions:6\n\nBillions:0 (since it's a 9-digit number)\n\nNow adding each column:\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\n1. Ones: 1 + 0 =1 \u2192 write 1, carry 0.\n\n2. Tens:7+6=13 \u2192 write 3, carry 1.\n\n3. Hundreds:4+9=13 +1=14 \u2192 write 4, carry1.\n\n4. Thousands:6+2=8 +1=9 \u2192 write9, carry0.\n\n5. Ten thousands:2+9=11 \u2192 write1, carry1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands:9+9=18 +1=19 \u2192 write9, carry1.\n\n7. Millions:5+4=9 +1=10 \u2192 write0, carry1.\n\n8. Ten millions:8+6=14 +1=15 \u2192 write5, carry1.\n\n9. Hundred millions:4+6=10 +1=11 \u2192 write1, carry1.\n\n10. Billions: carryover1 \u2192 write1.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\nOnes:1\n\nTens:3\n\nHundreds:4\n\nThousands:9\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nMillions:0\n\nTen millions:5\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nBillions:1\n\nPutting this together from highest to lowest place:\n\nBillions:1,\n\nHundred millions:1,\n\nTen millions:5,\n\nMillions:0,\n\nHundred thousands:9,\n\nTen th