+1 (carry) =12. So write 2, carryover1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):2+9=11 +1=12. Write2, carryover1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):7+0=7 +1 (carry)=8. Write8, carryover0.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):3+8=11. Since no carry from previous, it's 11. So write 1, carryover1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):4+7=11 +1 (carry)=12. Write2, carryover1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):5+0=5 +1=6, carryover0.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):2+0=2, no carry.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):3+2=5.\n\nNow compiling all the digits from right to left:.\n\nStarting from the first digit (position1):.\n\nThe digits written are:.\n\nPosition1:2.\n\nPosition2:2.\n\nPosition3:2.\n\nPosition4:8.\n\nPosition5:1.\n\nPosition6:2.\n\nPosition7:6.\n\nPosition8:2.\n\nPosition9:5.\n\nPlus the final carryover from position9? Wait, position9 (hundred millions) added to 3+2=5, no carryover.\n\nWait, but when we go through each position:.\n\nWait, the positions are from right (ones) to left (hundred millions). So the digits written are:.\n\nThe result digits, from right to left:.\n\nPosition1 (ones):2.\n\nPosition2 (tens):2.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):2.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):8.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):2.\n\nPosition7 (millions):6.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):2.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):5.\n\nBut we also have a carryover from position5 (ten thousands) which was 1, so that added to position6 (hundred thousands). Let me confirm:.\n\nWait, in position5 (ten thousands):.\n\n3 (from first number) +8 (from second) =11. So that gives a digit of 1 and carryover1 to the next higher place (hundred thousands).\n\nThen position6 (hundred thousands):4 +7 =11 plus the carryover1 =12. So that's 2 with carryover1 to the millions place.\n\nPosition7 (millions):5+0 +1 (carryover) =6, so no further carryover.\n\nSo the digits are indeed as above. Now, compiling all the digits from highest to lowest (left to right):.\n\nHundred millions:5.\n\nTen millions:2.\n\nMillions:6.\n\nHundred thousan