laces.\n\nLet me list each digit position with their place values:.\n\nStarting from the right (position 1 is ones):.\n\nNumber1: 521507157 digits are:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):7.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):5.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):7.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):0.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5.\n\nPosition7 (millions):1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):2.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):5.\n\nNumber2:702417128 digits:.\n\nPosition1:8.\n\nPosition2:2.\n\nPosition3:1.\n\nPosition4:7.\n\nPosition5:1.\n\nPosition6:4.\n\nPosition7:2.\n\nPosition8:0.\n\nPosition9:7.\n\nSo adding each position:.\n\nPosition1:7+8=15 → 5, carryover1.\n\nPosition2:5+2 +1=8 → 8, carryover0.\n\nPosition3:1+1=2 →2, carryover0.\n\nPosition4:7+7=14 →4, carryover1.\n\nPosition5:0+1 +1=2 →2, carryover0.\n\nPosition6:5+4=9 →9, carryover0.\n\nPosition7:1+2=3 →3, carryover0.\n\nPosition8:2+0=2 →2, carryover0.\n\nPosition9:5+7=12 →2, carryover1.\n\nNow, after the hundred millions place (position9), there's a carryover of 1, so we add a new digit (position10) which is 1.\n\nSo putting it all together, the digits from position10 down to position1 are:.\n\n1 (position10), 2 (position9), 2 (position8), 2 (position7?), wait let me list them properly.\n\nWait, the positions after adding:.\n\nThe result digits are:.\n\nPosition1:5.\n\nPosition2:8.\n\nPosition3:2.\n\nPosition4:4.\n\nPosition5:2.\n\nPosition6:9.\n\nPosition7:3.\n\nPosition8:2.\n\nPosition9:2 (since 5+7=12, so 2 here with carryover).\n\nPlus the carryover 1 in position10.\n\nSo the number is:.\n\nPosition10:1,.\n\nPosition9:2,.\n\nPosition8:2,.\n\nPosition7:3,.\n\nPosition6:9,.\n\nPosition5:2,.\n\nPosition4:4,.\n\nPosition3:2,.\n\nPosition2:8,.\n\nPosition1:5.\n\nWait, but when written out as a number, the highest digit is position10 (billions place). So the digits would be:.\n\n1 (billions), 2 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nWait that doesn't seem right. Let me reconstruct the number step by step.\n\nStarting from position1 (ones):5.\n\nPosition2 (tens):8.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):2.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):4.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):2.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):9.\n\nPosition7 (millions):3.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):2.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):2.\n\nPosition10 (billions):1.\n\nSo arranging from highest to lowest, the number is:.\n\n1 (billions), 2 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 5 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
