 1.\n\nHundreds: 4+0+1=5 → 5.\n\nThousands:5+0=5 →5.\n\nTen-thousands:6+6=12 →2 carry1.\n\nHundred-thousands:3+1+1=5 →5.\n\nMillions:4 (from first number's millions place?) Wait, maybe I messed up the place values here. Let me write down each number's digits with their places to be precise.\n\nWait, perhaps I should break down each number digit by digit:.\n\nFirst number: 443,365,463.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\nDigits from right to left (positions 1 to 9):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 3.\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 6.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):4.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):5.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):6.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):3.\n\nPosition 7 (millions):4.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):3.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):4.\n\nSecond number: 428,160,067.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\nPosition 1:7.\n\nPosition 2:6.\n\nPosition 3:0.\n\nPosition 4:0.\n\nPosition 5:6.\n\nPosition 6:1.\n\nPosition 7:8.\n\nPosition 8:2.\n\nPosition 9:4.\n\nNow adding each position:.\n\nPosition 1: 3 +7=10 → 0, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 2:6+6 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nPosition3:4+0 +1=5, no carryover.\n\nPosition4:5+0=5.\n\nPosition5:6+6=12 →2, carryover1.\n\nPosition6:3+1 +1=5, no carryover.\n\nPosition7:4+8=12 →2, carryover1.\n\nPosition8:3+2 +1=6, no carryover.\n\nPosition9:4+4=8.\n\nSo putting all together from right to left:.\n\nDigits are:.\n\nPosition1:0.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition3:5.\n\nPosition4:5.\n\nPosition5:2.\n\nPosition6:5.\n\nPosition7:2.\n\nPosition8:6.\n\nPosition9:8.\n\nSo the sum is 8 6 2 5 5 2 5 3 0 → Wait, no. Wait, when written from highest to lowest position, the digits would be:.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):8.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):6.\n\nPosition7 (millions):2.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):2.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):5.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):5.\n\nPosition2 (tens):3.\n\nPosition1 (ones):0.\n\nWait, that would make the number 862,525,530? Let me see:.\n\nBreaking it down:.\n\nHundred millions place:8.\n\nTen millions:6 → 860,000,0