1.\n\nTen millions:7 +7=14 plus1=15 →5, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:8 +7=15 plus1=16 →6, carryover1.\n\nBillions place: The carryover 1. So the total becomes 1 followed by the digits we have.\n\nWait, so let me retrace:.\n\nStarting from the right, each step's result:.\n\nOnes: 14 →4, carry 1.\n\nTens: 5+6+1=12 →2, carry1.\n\nHundreds:1+9+1=11 →1, carry1.\n\nThousands:3+4 +1=8 →8, carry0.\n\nTen thousands:7+6=13 →3, carry1.\n\nHundred thousands:4+6=10 +1=11 →1, carry1.\n\nMillions:4 (from first number) +5 (second number) +1 (carry)=10 →0, carry1.\n\nTen millions:7+7+1=15 →5, carry1.\n\nHundred millions:8+7=15 +1=16 →6, carry1.\n\nBillions: The carryover 1, so we have 1 in the billions place.\n\nPutting all together, starting from the right:.\n\nThe digits collected are:.\n\nOnes:4.\n\nTens:2.\n\nHundreds:1.\n\nThousands:8.\n\nTen thousands:3.\n\nHundred thousands:1.\n\nMillions:0.\n\nTen millions:5.\n\nHundred millions:6.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nSo the total is 1,650,318,124?.\n\nWait let me check again step by step:.\n\nLet me write the addition vertically:.\n\n          8 7 4 4 7 3 1 5 7.\n\n        + 7 7 5 6 6 4 9 6 7.\n\n        ---------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\n7 +7 =14 →4, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:5 +6 =11 +1 =12 →2, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:1+9=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nThousands:3+4=7 +1=8 →8, carryover0.\n\nTen thousands:7+6=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:4+6=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nMillions place:4 (from first number) +5 (second number) =9 +1 (carryover)=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:7 (first) +7 (second) =14 +1=15 →5, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:8 (first) +7 (second)=15 +1 (carryover) =16 →6, carryover1.\n\nBillions place: carryover1 remains, so we add 1 at the beginning.\n\nThus the total is 1 6 5 0 3 1 8 1 2 4 → which is 1,650,318,124?.\n\nWait, let me check the digits again:.\n\nThe digits from right to left:.\n\nOnes:4.\n\nTens:2.\n\nHundreds:1.\n\nThousands:8.\n\nTen thousands:3.\n\nHundred thousands:1.\n\nMillions:0.\n\nTen millions:5.\n\nHundred millions:6.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nSo written left to right, it's 1 (billions), 6 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 4 (ones). So 1,650,318,124.\n\nWait but let me confirm with another method. Let me add the numbers as whole numbers:.\n\n874,473,157 + 775,664,967.\n\nLet me compute this step by step.\n\nFirst, adding 874,473,157 and 700,000,000 gives 1,574,473,157. Then add 75,664,967.\n\nWait maybe that's more complicated. Alternatively, let me compute using another approach.\n\nAlternatively, adding 874,473,157 + 775,664,967:.\n\nBreak into parts:.\n\n800,000,000 + 700,000,000 = 1,500,000,000.\n\n74,473,157 + 75,664,967 = ?.\n\n74,473,157 +75,664,967:.\n\n74,473,157 +75,000,000 = 149,473,157.\n\nThen add 664,967: 149,473,157 + 664,967 = 150,138,124</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
