      "text": "1,645,000,000 + 628,608 = 1,645,628,608.\n\nWait a minute, this contradicts my previous result. Earlier step-by-step addition gave me 1,645,624,108, but this method gives 1,645,628,608. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nLet me recheck the first method's hundred thousands place. Wait in the first approach, when adding the hundred thousands place:\n\nThe original numbers: let me write them out with all digits:\n\nFirst number: 8 0 8 3 6 6 1 1 7\n\nSecond number: 8 3 7 2 6 2 4 9 1\n\nWait, perhaps I misaligned the digits. Let me write them properly with commas to see:\n\nFirst number: 808,366,117 \u2192 digits from left to right (billions down to ones):\n\nDigit positions (from right, starting at 1):\n\nPosition 9: 8 (hundred millions place)\nPosition 8: 0 (ten millions)\nPosition 7: 8 (millions)\nPosition 6: 3 (hundred thousands)\nPosition 5: 6 (ten thousands)\nPosition 4: 6 (thousands)\nPosition 3: 1 (hundreds)\nPosition 2: 1 (tens)\nPosition 1: 7 (ones)\n\nWait actually, maybe I messed up the digit positions. Let me write each number digit by digit.\n\nFirst number: 808,366,117 \u2192 digits are:\n\nDigit 1 (ones): 7\n\nDigit 2 (tens):1\n\nDigit 3 (hundreds):1\n\nDigit 4 (thousands):6\n\nDigit 5 (ten thousands):6\n\nDigit 6 (hundred thousands):3\n\nDigit 7 (millions):8\n\nDigit 8 (ten millions):0\n\nDigit 9 (hundred millions):8\n\nSecond number:837,262,491 \u2192 digits:\n\nDigit 1 (ones):1\n\nDigit 2 (tens):9\n\nDigit 3 (hundreds):4\n\nDigit 4 (thousands):2\n\nDigit 5 (ten thousands):6\n\nDigit 6 (hundred thousands):2\n\nDigit 7 (millions):7\n\nDigit 8 (ten millions):3\n\nDigit 9 (hundred millions):8\n\nSo when adding digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nDigit 1: 7 +1 =8 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nDigit 2 (tens):1 +9 =10 \u2192 0 carryover 1\n\nDigit3 (hundreds):1 +4 =5 plus carryover 1 \u21926? Wait, wait, earlier I thought digit3 was 6 here, but let's see:\n\nWait first number's hundreds place (digit3) is 1 (since fir