ns:6\n\n- Millions:7\n\n- Hundred thousands:1\n\n- Ten thousands:1\n\n- Thousands:9\n\n- Hundreds:2\n\n- Tens:1\n\n- Ones:4\n\nNow adding each place:\n\nStarting from Ones:\n\nOnes:3+4=7.\n\nTens:7+1=8.\n\nHundreds:8+2=10 \u2192 0, carry1.\n\nThousands:0 +9 +1(carry)=10 \u21920, carry1.\n\nTen thousands:8 +1 +1(carry)=10 \u21920, carry1.\n\nHundred thousands:6 +1 +1(carry)=8 \u21928, carry0.\n\nMillions:1 +7=8 \u21928.\n\nTen millions:2 +6=8 \u21928.\n\nHundred millions:7 +9=16 \u21926, carry1.\n\nBillions:0+0+1=1.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nBillions:1,\n\nHundred millions:6,\n\nTen millions:8,\n\nMillions:8,\n\nHundred thousands:8,\n\nTen thousands:0,\n\nThousands:0,\n\nHundreds:0,\n\nTens:8,\n\nOnes:7.\n\nThus, the number is 1,688,000,087. But when I added the parts separately, I thought it was 1,688,800,087. Wait, where did that come from?\n\nWait the separate addition:\n\nFirst number:721,680,873\n\nSecond number:967,119,214.\n\nAdding:\n\n721,680,873\n\n+967,119,214\n\nLet me add step by step:\n\nStart with 721,680,873 + 900,000,000 = 1,621,680,873\n\nThen add 67,119,214:\n\n1,621,680,873 + 60,000,000 = 1,681,680,873\n\nThen add 7,119,214:\n\n1,681,680,873 +7,000,000 =1,688,680,873\n\nThen add 119,214:\n\n1,688,680,873 + 100,000 =1,688,780,873\n\n+19,214 \u21921,688,780,873 +19,214 =1,688,800,087.\n\nAh, so there is a discrepancy between the two methods. Which one is correct?\n\nWait in the digit-by-digit method, the hundred thousands place was 8, but in the separate addition, the total is 1,688,800,087, which has an 8 in the hundred thousands place, and the ten thousands place is 0. Wait let's see the number 1,688,800,087.\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n1 (billions),\n\n6 (hundred millions),\n\n8 (ten millions),\n\n8 (millions),\n\n8 (hundred thousands),\n\n8 (ten thousands),\n\n0 (thousands),\n\n0 (hundreds),\n\n0 (tens),\n\n7 (ones). Wait no, that can't be. Wait let me parse the number correctly.\n\nWait 1,688,800,087:\n\n- 1,688,800,087 \u2192 commas after every three digits from the right.\n\nSo it's 1,688,800,087 \u2192 1 billion, 688 million, 800 thousand, and 87. Wait no, let's separate:\n\nIt should be 1,688,800,087 \u2192 1 (billions), 688 (millions?), but commas are placed as 1,688,800,087 \u2192 actually, in standard format, it's 1,688,800,087 \u2192 1 billion, 688 million, 800 thousand, 87. But breaking down:\n\n- 1,688,800,087 \u2192 1 (billion), 688 (million), 800 (thousand), 087.\n\nBut the digit-by-digit method gives 1,688,000,087 \u2192 which would be 1,688,000,087 \u2192 1 billion, 688 million, 0 thousand, 87. But according to the separate addition, it's 1,688,800,087.\n\nThis inconsistency must be resolved. Where is the error?\n\nWait let me do the addition manually:\n\nFirst number:721,680,873\n\nSecond number:967,119,214\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n3+4=7 (ones).\n\n7+1=8 (tens).\n\n8+2=10 \u2192 write 0, carryover1 (hundreds).\n\n0 (thousands place of first) +9 (second) +1 (carry)=10 \u2192 write0, carryover1 (thousands).\n\n8 (ten thousands place of first?) Wait wait, let me write the numbers vertically:\n\n        721,680,873\n\n      +967,119,214\n\n      =============\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nOnes:3+4=7\n\nTens:7+1=8\n\nHundreds:8+2=10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nThousands:0 +9 +1(carry)=10 \u2192 0, carry1\n\nTen thousands:8 (from first number's ten thousands place?) Wait let's look at the numbers:\n\nFirst number's digits from right:\n\nPosition0:3 (ones)\n\nPosition1:7 (tens)\n\nPosition2:8 (hundreds)\n\nPosition3:0 (thousands)\n\nPosition4:8 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition5:6 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition6:1 (millions)\n\nPosition7:2 (ten millions)\n\nPosition8:7 (hundred millions)\n\nSecond number:\n\nPosition0:4\n\nPosition1:1\n\nPosition2:2\n\nPosition3:9 (thousands)\n\nPosition4:1 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition5:1 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition6:7 (millions)\n\nPosition7:6 (ten millions)\n\nPosition8:9 (hundred millions)\n\nSo ten thousands place (position4):\n\nFirst number has 8, second has1 \u2192 8+1 + carryover1 (from thousands) =10 \u2192 write0, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands (position5):\n\nFirst has6, second has1 \u21926+1 +carryover1=8 \u2192 no carryover.\n\nMillions (position6):1+7=8.\n\nTen millions (position7):2+6=8.\n\nHundred millions (position8):7+9=16 \u21926 with carryover1.\n\nBillions (position9):1.\n\nThus the total is 1,688,000,087. So the previous separate addition was wrong. Where did I go wrong in the separate addition?\n\nAh, I see. When I added 721,680,873 + 967,119,214:\n\nLet me do it step by step:\n\n721,680,873\n\n+967,119,214\n\nAdding the units:\n\n3 +4 =7\n\n7 +1 =8\n\n8 +2 =10 \u2192 0, carryover1\n\n0 +9 +1 =10 \u21920, carryover1\n\n8 +1 +1 =10 \u21920, carryover1\n\n6 +1 +1 =8 \u2192 no carryover.\n\n1 +7 =8\n\n2 +6 =8\n\n7 +9 =16 \u21926, carryover1.\n\nAdding the carryover gives 1 at the beginning.\n\nSo total is 1,688,000,087. Thus, the user's answer of 1,678,800,087 is incorrect. The correct answer should be 1,688,000,087.\n\nWait but the user's answer was 1,678,800,087. So perhaps they made an error in their calculation. The digit-by-digit method clearly shows it's 1,688,000,087.\n\nWait let me check with another approach: using calculator-like addition.\n\nFirst number:721,680,873\n\nSecond number:967,119,214\n\nAdding:\n\nStart with the first number: 721,680,873\n\nAdd 900,000,000 \u2192 1,621,680,873\n\nAdd 67,000,000 \u2192 1,688,680,873\n\nAdd 119,214 \u2192 1,688,680,873 +119,214 = ?\n\n1,688,680,873 +100,000 =1,688,780,873\n\n+19,214 \u2192 1,688,780,873 +19,214 = 1,688,800,087.\n\nWait this contradicts the digit-by-digit result. What's the issue here?\n\nWait, no, let's do the addition properly:\n\nAdding 721,680,873 +967,119,214:\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n        721,680,873\n\n      +967,119,214\n\n      =============\n\nAdding the digits:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:3+4=7.\n\nTens:7+1=8.\n\nHundreds:8+2=10 \u2192 0, carryover1.\n\nThousands:0+9+1=10 \u21920, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:8+1+1=10 \u21920, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:6+1+1=8 \u2192 no carryover.\n\nMillions:1+7=8.\n\nTen millions:2+6=8.\n\nHundred millions:7+9=16 \u21926, carryover1.\n\nBillions:0+0+1=1.\n\nThus the total is 1,688,000,087.\n\nBut in the separate addition approach where I broke it down into adding 900 million, etc., I must have made an error. Let me check that again:\n\nStarting with 721,680,873 +967,119,214.\n\nLet me break it into 700,000,000 +21,680,873 and 900,000,000 +67,119,214.\n\nAdding 700M +900M =1,600,000,000.\n\nAdding 21,680,873 +67,119,214:\n\n21,680,873 +60,000,000 =81,680,873.\n\n81,680,873 +7,119,214 =88,800,087.\n\nThen total is 1,600,000,000 +88,800,087 =1,688,800,087.\n\nWait now this contradicts the digit-by-digit result. What's happening here?\n\nWait this is confusing. Let me use a calculator to verify.\n\nCalculating 721,680,873 +967,119,214:\n\n721,680,873 +967,119,214.\n\nAdding the two numbers:\n\nLet me compute 721,680,873 + 967,119,214.\n\nAdding the units:\n\n721,680,873\n\n+967,119,214\n\n= (700,000,000 + 21,680,873) + (900,000,000 +67,119,214)\n\n= 1,600,000,000 + (21,680,873 +67,119,214).\n\n21,680,873 +67,119,214:\n\n21,680,873 +60,000,000 =81,680,873\n\n81,680,873 +7,119,214 = 88,800,087.\n\nThus total is 1,600,000,000 +88,800,087 =1,688,800,087.\n\nBut the digit-by-digit addition gives 1,688,000,087. There's a discrepancy of 800,000.\n\nWait where is the mistake?\n\nWait let me do the digit-by-digit again very carefully:\n\nLet me write the numbers aligned:\n\n          721,680,873\n\n        + 967,119,214\n\n        =============\n\nLet me write them without commas:\n\n721680873\n\n+967119214\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right (units):\n\nPosition0:3+4=7\n\nPosition1:7+1=8\n\nPosition2:8+2=10 \u2192 0 carry1\n\nPosition3:0+9+1=10 \u21920 carry1\n\nPosition4:8+1+1=10 \u21920 carry1\n\nPosition5:6+1+1=8 \u21928 carry0\n\nPosition6:1+7=8\n\nPosition7:2+6=8\n\nPosition8:7+9=16 \u21926 carry1\