tion, it should be 1,688,800,087 \u2192 which is 1 billion, 688 million, 800 thousand, 87.\n\nAh! So the digit-by-digit method missed adding the 800,000 part. Where did that happen?\n\nLet me re-express the digit-by-digit addition:\n\nAfter adding all positions:\n\nThe digits from billions down:\n\n1 (billions),\n\n6 (hundred millions),\n\n8 (ten millions),\n\n8 (millions),\n\n8 (hundred thousands),\n\n0 (ten thousands),\n\n0 (thousands),\n\n0 (hundreds),\n\n8 (tens),\n\n7 (ones).\n\nWait that would make the number:\n\n1,688,800,087.\n\nWait hold on! I think I made a mistake in the digit positions earlier.\n\nLet me list the digits with their correct place values:\n\nPosition9:1 (billions)\n\nPosition8:6 (hundred millions)\n\nPosition7:8 (ten millions)\n\nPosition6:8 (millions)\n\nPosition5:8 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition4:0 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition3:0 (thousands)\n\nPosition2:0 (hundreds)\n\nPosition1:8 (tens)\n\nPosition0:7 (ones)\n\nSo arranging them:\n\nBillions:1,\n\nHundred millions:6,\n\nTen millions:8,\n\nMillions:8,\n\nHundred thousands:8,\n\nTen thousands:0,\n\nThousands:0,\n\nHundreds:0,\n\nTens:8,\n\nOnes:7.\n\nThus the number is 1,688,800,087.\n\nWait aha! I must have miscounted the positions earlier. The hundred thousands digit is position5, which is 8, so that's the fifth digit from the right (since position0 is ones). Let's see:\n\nThe number is:\n\nDigit positions:\n\nPosition9:1,\n\n8:6,\n\n7:8,\n\n6:8,\n\n5:8,\n\n4:0,\n\n3:0,\n\n2:0,\n\n1:8,\n\n0:7.\n\nSo writing them from left (billions) to right (ones):\n\n1 (billions),\n\n6 (hundred millions),\n\n8 (ten millions),\n\n8 (millions),\n\n8 (hundred thousands),\n\n0 (ten thousands),\n\n0 (thousands),\n\n0 (hundreds),\n\n8 (tens),\n\n7 (ones).\n\nThus the number is indeed 1,688,800,087. So my earlier mistake was in interpreting the digits after the digit-by-digit calculation. I had mistakenly thought the hundred thousands digit was in a different place.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 1,688,