followed by the rest. Let me check again step by step to ensure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nWait, maybe I should list each digit position clearly. Let me write both numbers with their digits:.\n\nFirst number: 4 6 0 7 8 8 2 0 5  .\nSecond number:7 6 7 4 6 4 5 7 8  .\nWait, actually, let me confirm the digit positions. Let's count the digits properly. .\n\n460,788,205 is 9 digits: 4 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\n767,464,578 is also 9 digits: 7 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nAdding digit by digit from right to left:.\n\nOnes: 5 +8=13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nTens:0+7=7 +1=8. So 8, no carry.\n\nHundreds:2+5=7. So 7.\n\nThousands:8+4=12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands:8 +6=14 +1=15. Write 5, carry1.\n\nHundred thousands:7 +4=11 +1=12. Write 2, carry1.\n\nMillions:0 +7=7 +1=8. Write8, no carry.\n\nTen millions:6 +6=12. Write2, carry1.\n\nHundred millions:4 +7=11 +1=12. Write 2, carry1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
