\nWait, let me write them vertically:.\n\n        3 0 0 5 8 8 7 7 2.\n\n      + 4 4 0 0 9 1 7 6 9.\n\n      ---------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\n2 + 9 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nNext, tens place: 7 + 6 =13 +1 =14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place: 7 +7 =14 +1 =15. Wait, wait, hold on. Wait the hundreds place in the first number is the third digit from the right? Let me confirm the positions again. Let me write each digit's position properly:.\n\nLet me label the digits from right to left (starting at position 1):.\n\nFirst number: positions 1-9:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 2.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):7.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):7.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):8.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):8.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5.\n\nPosition7 (millions):0.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):0.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):3.\n\nSecond number:.\n\nPosition1:9.\n\nPosition2:6.\n\nPosition3:7.\n\nPosition4:1.\n\nPosition5:9.\n\nPosition6:0.\n\nPosition7:4.\n\nPosition8:4.\n\nPosition9:4.\n\nWait, that's probably where I made a mistake earlier. Let me re-express the numbers properly.\n\nWait maybe it's better to write both numbers digit by digit in columns:.\n\nLet me write the numbers as:.\n\nFirst number: 3 0 0 5 8 8 7 7 2.\n\nSecond number:4 4 0 0 9 1 7 6 9.\n\nAligning each digit from left to right as hundred millions down to ones.\n\nWait, actually, in standard notation, the first digit is the highest place. So the first number is:.\n\n3 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 2 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 4 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 9 (ones).\n\nSo when adding vertically:.\n\nHundred millions: 3 +4 =7.\n\nTen millions:0 +4=4.\n\nMillions:0 +0=0.\n\nHundred thousands:5 +0=5.\n\nTen thousands:8 +9=17. Wait, that's where a carryover would happen.\n\nWait, perhaps I should proceed step by step properly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 2 +9=11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:7 (from first number) +6 (from second) =13, plus the 1 carried over is 14. So 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:7 +7 =14, plus 1 is 15. So 5, carryover1.\n\nThousands place:8 +1 =9, plus 1 is 10. So write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place:8 +9=17, plus 1 is 18. Write 8, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands place:5 +0=5 plus 1 is 6, no carryover.\n\nMillions place:0 +0=0.\n\nTen millions place:0 +4=4.\n\nHundred millions place:3 +4=7.\n\nWait, so putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the ones:1, then 4 (tens), 5 (hundreds), 0 (thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 6 (hundred thousands), 0 (millions),4 (ten millions),7 (hundred millions)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
