he previous step?), let's see:.\n\nWait let's go step by step through each position again carefully:.\n\nLet me make a table for each position:.\n\nPosition | First Number | Second Number | Sum (including carryover) | Digit | Carryover.\n---|---|---|---|---|---.\n1 (ones) |6 |7 |6+7=13 |3 |1.\n2 (tens)|9 |4 |9+4+1=14 |4 |1.\n3 (hundreds)|6 |0 |6+0+1=7 |7 |0.\n4 (thousands)|4 |0 |4+0=4 |4 |0.\n5 (ten thousands)|4 |0 |4+0=4 |4 |0.\n6 (hundred thousands)|1 |4 |1+4=5 |5 |0.\n7 (millions)|6 |4 |6+4=10 |0 |1.\n8 (ten millions)|9 |9 |9+9+1=19 |9 |1.\n9 (hundred millions)|5 |9 |5+9+1=15 |5 |1.\n\nAfter the last position (hundred millions), we still have a carryover of 1. So this carryover becomes a new digit to the left, making the total number of digits 10. Therefore, the final digits from right to left are:.\n\n3 (ones),4,7,4,4,5,0,9,5 and then the carryover 1. So the total is 1 followed by the digits 5,9,0,5,4,4,7,4,3.\n\nWait, let me reconstruct the final number:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position1) to the left:.\n\nPosition1:3.\n\nPosition2:4.\n\nPosition3:7.\n\nPosition4:4.\n\nPosition5:4.\n\nPosition6:5.\n\nPosition7:0.\n\nPosition8:9.\n\nPosition9:5.\n\nAnd then the carryover1 becomes position10:1.\n\nSo putting them all together from left (highest place) to right (ones):.\n\nPosition10:1 (billions place),.\n\nPosition9:5 (hundred millions),.\n\nPosition8:9 (ten millions),.\n\nPosition7:0 (millions),.\n\nPosition6:5 (hundred thousands),.\n\nPosition5:4 (ten thousands),.\n\nPosition4:4 (thousands),.\n\nPosition3:7 (hundreds),.\n\nPosition2:4 (tens),.\n\nPosition1:3 (ones).\n\nSo the number is 1,590,544,743.\n\nWait, let me write that out with commas:.\n\n1,590,544,743.\n\nWait, let me verify this by adding the numbers in another way.\n\nAlternatively, adding 596,144,696 + 994,400,407.\n\nLet me use another method: rounding or breaking into parts.\n\n596,144,696 + 994,400,407.\n\nAdd the millions first:.\n\n596,144,696 = 596,000,000 + 144,696.\n\n994,400,407 = 994,000,000 + 400,407.\n\nAdding the millions parts: 596,000,000 + 994,000,000 = 1,590,000,000.\n\nThen add the smaller parts: 144,696 + 400,407.\n\n144,696 + 400,407:.\n\n144,696 + 400,000 = 544,696.\n\nThen add 407: 544,696 + 407 = 545,103</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
