103), which overflows into the millions place. Therefore, the small parts addition's result must be added to the large parts while considering that the small parts can carry over into the millions.\n\nWait the large parts were596,000,000 +994,000,000 =1,590,000,000.\n\nThe small parts are144,696 +400,407 =545,103.\n\nAdding these together:\n\n1,590,000,000 +545,103 =1,590,545,103.\n\nThis is correct because the small parts' total (545,103) doesn't overflow into the millions place (since it's less than a million). Therefore, the digit-by-digit method must be incorrect.\n\nBut why? Let's re-express the digit-by-digit result:\n\n1,590,544,743 versus1,590,545,103.\n\nThe difference is in the thousands and hundreds places: 544,743 vs545,103.\n\nLooking at the thousands and hundreds digits:\n\nIn the digit-by-digit:\n\nThousands:4, hundreds:7.\n\nIn the correct total: thousands:5, hundreds:1.\n\nAh! The hundreds digit in the digit-by-digit is7, but in the correct total it's1. This indicates that in the digit-by-digit process, there was an error in the hundreds place.\n\nWait in the digit-by-digit steps:\n\nPosition3 (hundreds) was6 (first number's hundreds digit) +0 (second's) +1 (carryover from tens) =7 \u2192 correct.\n\nPosition4 (thousands) is4 \u2192 correct.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands) is4.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands) is5.\n\nPosition7 (millions) is0.\n\nSo the millions digit is0, but in the correct total it's5 (from the small parts addition's hundred thousands place). Wait the millions digit in the full digit-by-digit is0, but in the correct total it's5.\n\nWait this is a major discrepancy. The millions digit in the digit-by-digit result is0 (from position7), but in the correct total it's5. That means there's a big mistake in the digit-by-digit steps.\n\nWait let me check position7 (millions place):\n\nFirst number's millions digit is6 (from596,144,696 \u2192 the millions digit is the seventh position from the right, which is6).\n\nSecond number's millions digit is4 (from994,400,407 \u2192 seventh position from the right is4).\n\nAdding them:6+4=10 \u21920 with carryover1. That's correct. So millions digit is0, and carryover1 to the next (ten millions) place.\n\nBut in the correct total (1,590,545,103), the millions digit is5. Wait the total is1,590,545,103.\n\nBreaking this down:\n\nBillions:1,\n\nHundred millions:5,\n\nTen millions:9,\n\nMillions:0,\n\nHundred thousands:5,\n\nTen thousands:4,\n\nThousands:5,\n\nHundreds:1,\n\nTens:0,\n\nOnes:3.\n\nAh! The millions digit is0, which matches the digit-by-digit result. So why does the small parts addition contribute to the millions place?\n\nThe small parts addition (545,103) doesn't reach the millions place (which is the seventh digit from the right), so the millions digit in the total should indeed be0, as per digit-by-digit. But according to the breakdown method, the total is1,590,545,103, where the millions digit is0 (since the number is1,590,545,103 \u2192 the millions digit is the seventh digit from the right, which is0 (since it's ...545,103). Wait, let's count:\n\n1,590,545,103:\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n1 (billion),\n\n5 (hundred millions),\n\n9 (ten millions),\n\n0 (millions),\n\n5 (hundred thousands),\n\n4 (ten thousands),\n\n5 (thousands),\n\n1 (hundreds),\n\n0 (tens),\n\n3 (ones).\n\nYes, the millions digit is0, which matches the digit-by-digit result. The confusion was from my earlier incorrect interpretation of the breakdown method's result. The correct total is indeed1,590,544,743 according to digit-by-digit, but the breakdown method also gives1,590,545,103. There's a discrepancy of360.\n\nWait let's look at both results:\n\nDigit-by-digit result:1,590,544,743.\n\nBreakdown result:1,590,545,103.\n\nSubtracting the two:1,590,545,103 -1,590,544,743=360.\n\nThe difference is in the thousands and hundreds places: the digit-by-digit has44,743 in the last five digits, while the breakdown has5,103 in the last four digits of the small parts (which is part of the tot