herefore, in position4 (thousands place):.\n\n1 (first) +9 (second) +1 (carryover) =11. So write 1, carryover1.\n\nWait, I must have made a mistake earlier when I thought it was 5. That was the error. So position4 is actually 1+9 +1=11, so write 1 and carryover1.\n\nContinuing:.\n\nPosition4 result:1, carryover1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands place):.\n\nFirst number's ten thousands digit:7.\n\nSecond's ten thousands digit:3.\n\n7+3=10, plus carryover1 →11. So write1, carryover1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands place):.\n\nFirst's hundred thousands digit:0.\n\nSecond's:6.\n\n0+6=6 +1 (carryover) →7, carryover0.\n\nPosition7 (millions place):.\n\nFirst's millions digit:7.\n\nSecond's millions digit:5.\n\n7+5=12. No carryover yet. So 12 → write2, carryover1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions place):.\n\nFirst's ten millions:3.\n\nSecond's ten millions:1.\n\n3+1=4 + carryover1 →5, carryover0.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions place):.\n\nFirst's:1.\n\nSecond's:6 →1+6=7.\n\nNow, compiling all the results from right to left:.\n\nPositions 1-9 (from right to left):.\n\nPosition1:0.\n\nPosition2:2.\n\nPosition3:6.\n\nPosition4:1.\n\nPosition5:1.\n\nPosition6:7.\n\nPosition7:2.\n\nPosition8:5.\n\nPosition9:7.\n\nWait, let's list them in order from the highest place to the lowest (left to right):.\n\nThe hundred millions place (position9) is 7,.\n\nten millions (position8):5,.\n\nmillions (position7):2,.\n\nhundred thousands (position6):7,.\n\nten thousands (position5):1,.\n\nthousands (position4):1,.\n\nhundreds (position3):6,.\n\ntens (position2):2,.\n\nones (position1):0.\n\nSo putting them together:.\n\n7 (hundred millions),.\n\n5 (ten millions),.\n\n2 (millions),.\n\n7 (hundred thousands),.\n\n1 (ten thousands),.\n\n1 (thousands),.\n\n6 (hundreds),.\n\n2 (tens),.\n\n0 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
