lace: The carried over 1. Since there are no more digits, we just add that 1 at the beginning.\n\nPutting all together, starting from the ones digit: 8, then 9, 0, 5, 1, 0, 6, 3, 0, and the leading 1. Wait, let me check the positions again to make sure I didn't miscount the places.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the positions. Let me recount the digits step by step properly. Let me write each digit one by one with their place values.\n\nFirst number: 226,798,201. Breaking down each digit from right to left (since addition starts from the right):.\n\nPositions (starting at 0 for the ones place):.\n\n0: 1.\n1: 0.\n2: 2.\n3: 8.\n4: 9.\n5: 7.\n6: 6.\n7: 2.\n8: 2.\n\nSecond number: 809,216,897:.\n\n0:7.\n1:9.\n2:8.\n3:6.\n4:1.\n5:2.\n6:9.\n7:0.\n8:8.\n\nWait, maybe I need to align them properly. Let me list all digits with their place values:.\n\nFirst number (226,798,201):.\n\nDigit positions (right to left):.\n\nPosition 0 (ones): 1.\nPosition 1 (tens): 0.\nPosition 2 (hundreds): 2.\nPosition 3 (thousands): 8.\nPosition 4 (ten thousands): 9.\nPosition 5 (hundred thousands): 7.\nPosition 6 (millions): 6.\nPosition 7 (ten millions): 2.\nPosition 8 (hundred millions): 2.\n\nSecond number (809,216,897):.\n\nPosition 0 (ones):7.\nPosition 1 (tens):9.\nPosition 2 (hundreds):8.\nPosition 3 (thousands):6.\nPosition 4 (ten thousands):1.\nPosition 5 (hundred thousands):2.\nPosition 6 (millions):9.\nPosition 7 (ten millions):0.\nPosition 8 (hundred millions):8.\n\nNow, adding each position:.\n\nStarting at position 0:.\n\n1 +7 =8 (no carryover).\n\nPosition 1: 0 +9 =9 (no carryover).\n\nPosition 2:2 +8=10 → write 0, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 3:8 +6 =14 plus carryover 1=15 → write 5, carryover 1.\n\nPosition4:9 +1=10 plus carryover 1=11 → write 1, carryover1.\n\nPosition5:7 +2=9 plus carryover1=10 → write0, carryover1.\n\nPosition6:6 +9=15 plus carryover1=16 → write6, carryover1.\n\nPosition7:2 +0=2 plus carryover1=3 → write3, no carryover.\n\nPosition8:2 +8=10 → write0, carryover1.\n\