t column being added, not including the carryover? Like for the first step, the ones digits are 7 and 8, so "The ones place: 7 + 8". Then the next step, tens place digits, which are 7 and 1 (from the second number\'s tens place?), etc. Wait, need to confirm the exact digits in each place.\n\nWait let me parse the numbers properly. Let me write both numbers with their digits separated by commas for clarity:.\n\nFirst number: 758,930,577. Breaking down each digit from right to left:.\n\nPositions (starting from 0 for the rightmost):.\n\n- Position 0 (ones): 7.\n- Position 1 (tens): 7.\n- Position 2 (hundreds): 5.\n- Position 3 (thousands): 0.\n- Position 4 (ten thousands): 3.\n- Position 5 (hundred thousands): 9.\n- Position 6 (millions): 8.\n- Position 7 (ten millions): 5.\n- Position 8 (hundred millions): 7.\n\nSecond number: 819,849,018. Breaking down similarly:.\n\n- Position 0 (ones): 8.\n- Position 1 (tens): 1.\n- Position 2 (hundreds): 0.\n- Position 3 (thousands): 9.\n- Position 4 (ten thousands): 4.\n- Position 5 (hundred thousands): 8.\n- Position 6 (millions): 1.\n- Position 7 (ten millions): 9.\n- Position 8 (hundred millions): 8.\n- Position 9 (billions): 8 (Wait, actually, the second number is 819,849,018 which is 9 digits, so the highest place is hundred millions (position 8) with 8, and the next digit is 1 in the ten millions? Wait let me count again.\n\nWait, 819,849,018: Let\'s parse each digit:.\n\nFrom right to left:.\n\nDigits: 8 (position 0), 1 (1), 0 (2), 9 (3), 4 (4), 8 (5), 1 (6), 9 (7), 8 (8). Wait, the number is 819,849,018. Breaking into groups:.\n\n819,849,018 → 8 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 8 (ones). Wait no, commas are placed every three digits. So 819,849,018 is:.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\n- 819 (million part), then 849 (thousands), then 018. Wait:.\n\nActually, the number is written as 819,849,018. So:.\n\n- The first comma separates millions: 819, so 819 million.\n\nThen the next comma separates thousands: 849 thousand, and then 018. So digits:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nPosition 0: 8 (ones).\n\nPosition 1: 1 (tens).\n\nPosition 2: 0 (hundreds).\n\nPosition 3: 9 (thousands).\n\nPosition 4: 4 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition 5: 8 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition 6: 1 (millions).\n\nPosition 7: 1 (ten millions)? Wait no:.\n\nWait, 819,849,018:.\n\nBreaking down each digit:.\n\nStarting from the left:.\n\nDigit 1: 8 (hundred millions place).\n\nDigit 2: 1 (ten millions).\n\nDigit 3: 9 (millions).\n\nDigit 4: 8 (hundred thousands).\n\nDigit 5: 4 (ten thousands).\n\nDigit 6: 9 (thousands).\n\nDigit 7: 0 (hundreds).\n\nDigit 8: 1 (tens).\n\nDigit 9: 8 (ones).\n\nWait that\'s probably the correct breakdown. Let me write both numbers digit by digit:.\n\nFirst number: 758,930,577.\n\nDigits from right to left (positions 0 to 8):.\n\nPosition 0: 7 (ones).\n\n1:7 (tens).\n\n2:5 (hundreds).\n\n3:0 (thousands).\n\n4:3 (ten thousands).\n\n5:9 (hundred thousands).\n\n6:8 (millions).\n\n7:5 (ten millions).\n\n8:7 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 819,849,018.\n\nDigits from right to left (positions 0 to 8):.\n\nPosition 0:8 (ones).\n\n1:1 (tens).\n\n2:0 (hundreds).\n\n3:9 (thousands).\n\n4:4 (ten thousands).\n\n5:8 (hundred thousands).\n\n6:1 (millions).\n\n7:9 (ten millions).\n\n8:8 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, but the second number has 9 digits, so the highest position is 8 (hundred millions). The first number is also 9 digits (758,930,577 → 7 hundred millions, etc.). .\n\nNow, let\'s add them digit by digit starting from the right (position 0) to the left, keeping track of carryover.\n\nStarting with position 0 (ones):.\n\nDigit1 (first number):7, Digit2 (second number):8 → 7 +8=15. So write down 5, carryover 1 to next position.\n\nPosition 1 (tens):.\n\nDigits:7 (from first) +1 (from second) = 8, plus carryover 1 → total 9. No carryover.\n\nPosition 2 (hundreds):.\n\n5 (first) +0 (second) =5. No carryo