llions digit is1 (position6). So 8+1=9, plus carryover1 from hundred thousands place (which was 9+8=17 \u2192 carryover1). So 9+1=10 \u21920 with carryover1. So that's correct.\n\nTen millions place (position7): first number's digit is5 (ten millions), second's is9 (ten millions). 5+9=14 plus carryover1 is15 \u21925, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions (position8): first is7, second is8 \u219215 plus carryover1 is16 \u21926, carryover1.\n\nThen billions place: the carryover1 \u2192 total 1 at billions.\n\nThus, the total is 1,650,779,595.\n\nBut the user's answer was 1,578,778,595. Hmm, there's a discrepancy here. So perhaps I made a mistake, or the user's answer is wrong?\n\nWait let me use another method. Let's compute 758,930,577 + 819,849,018.\n\nLet me convert to numbers:\n\n758,930,577 + 819,849,018.\n\nAdding the two:\n\n758,930,577\n\n+819,849,018\n\n= ?\n\nLet me compute step by step:\n\n700,000,000 + 800,000,000 =1,500,000,000.\n\n58,000,000 +19,000,000 =77,000,000 \u2192 total 1,577,000,000.\n\n930,000 +849,000 =1,779,000 \u2192 total 1,578,779,000.\n\n577 +18 =595 \u2192 total 1,578,779,595.\n\nAh! Wait, so this gives 1,578,779,595. But my previous digit-wise calculation gave 1,650,779,595. There's a conflict here. I must have messed up the digit positions in the first calculation.\n\nWait let me check again where the mistake is.\n\nAh! Here's the error. When I broke down the first number into digits, I must have misassigned the positions. Let me re-express both numbers properly.\n\nFirst number: 758,930,577.\n\nBreaking down each digit from right (position0):\n\nPosition0:7 (ones).\n\nPosition1:7 (tens).\n\nPosition2:5 (hundreds).\n\nPosition3:0 (thousands).\n\nPosition4:3 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition5:9 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition6:8 (millions).\n\nPosition7:5 (ten millions).\n\nPosition8:7 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number:819,849,018.\n\nPosition0:8 (ones).\n\nPosition1:1 (tens).\n\nPosition2:0 (hundreds).\n\nPosition3:9 (thousands).\n\nPosition4:4 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition5:8 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition6:1 (millions).\n\nPosition7:9 (ten millions).\n\nPosition8:8 (hundred millions).\n\nNow, let's recompute step by step:\n\nStarting from position0:\n\n0:7+8=15 \u21925, carry1.\n\n1:7+1+1=9 \u21929, carry0.\n\n2:5+0=5.\n\n3:0+9=9.\n\n4:3+4=7.\n\n5:9+8=17 \u21927, carry1.\n\n6:8+1 +1 (carry)=10 \u21920, carry1.\n\n7:5+9 +1 (carry)=15 \u21925, carry1.\n\n8:7+8 +1 (carry)=16 \u21926, carry1.\n\nThen the final carryover1 \u2192 so total digits are 1 (billions) followed by 6 (hundred millions), then the rest.\n\nWait that gives 1,650,779,595 again. But the other method gives 1,578,779,595. Which is correct?\n\nWait let me use calculator verification:\n\nLet me compute 758,930,577 + 819,849,018.\n\nAdding the two:\n\n758,930,577 + 819,849,018.\n\nLet me add 758,930,577 + 800,000,000 =1,558,930,577.\n\nThen add the remaining 19,849,018.\n\n1,558,930,577 +19,849,018 = ?\n\n1,558,930,577 +10,000,000 =1,568,930,577.\n\n+9,849,018 \u2192 1,568,930,577 +9,849,018.\n\nAdding 9,000,000 \u21921,577,930,577.\n\n+849,018 \u21921,577,930,577 +849,018 =1,578,779,595.\n\nAh! So the correct answer is 1,578,779,595. So where did I go wrong in the first digit-wise approach?\n\nAh, I see. In the digit positions, when I was adding the hundred millions place, I must have miscalculated.\n\nLet me redo the digit-by-digit addition carefully:\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):\n\nFirst number's digit:7, second's digit:8 \u21927+8=15. Then add any carryover from previous?\n\nWait let's go step by step again:\n\nStarting from position0 to position8.\n\nPosition0 (ones): 7+8=15 \u21925, carry1.\n\nPosition1 (tens):7+1=8 +1(carry)=9 \u21929, carry0.\n\nPosition2 (hundreds):5+0=5 \u21925, carry0.\n\nPosition3 (thousands):0+9=9 \u21929, carry0.\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):3+4=7 \u21927, carry0.\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands):9+8=17 \u21927, carry1.\n\nPosition6 (millions):8 (first) +1 (second)=9 \u21929 + carry1=10 \u21920, carry1.\n\