ommas are separating the groups. Let's write it as:\n\n819,849,018 \u2192 8 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nTherefore, the millions digit (position6) is9 (the third digit from left), and the hundred thousands digit (position5) is8 (fourth digit).\n\nSo in position6 (millions place) of the second number is9, not1. That's where the mistake was!\n\nOh no! I had misassigned the digits for the second number. Earlier, I thought the millions digit was1, but actually it's9. So that's the error.\n\nLet me redo the digit-by-digit addition correctly now.\n\nFirst number:758,930,577.\n\nDigits from position0 (right) to position8 (left):\n\nPosition0:7 (ones),\n\nPosition1:7 (tens),\n\nPosition2:5 (hundreds),\n\nPosition3:0 (thousands),\n\nPosition4:3 (ten thousands),\n\nPosition5:9 (hundred thousands),\n\nPosition6:8 (millions),\n\nPosition7:5 (ten millions),\n\nPosition8:7 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number:819,849,018.\n\nDigits from position0 to position8:\n\nPosition0:8 (ones),\n\nPosition1:1 (tens),\n\nPosition2:0 (hundreds),\n\nPosition3:9 (thousands),\n\nPosition4:4 (ten thousands),\n\nPosition5:8 (hundred thousands),\n\nPosition6:9 (millions),\n\nPosition7:1 (ten millions),\n\nPosition8:8 (hundred millions).\n\nNow, let's recompute:\n\nStarting from position0:\n\n0:7+8=15 \u21925, carry1.\n\n1:7+1 +1=9 \u21929, carry0.\n\n2:5+0=5 \u21925.\n\n3:0+9=9 \u21929.\n\n4:3+4=7 \u21927.\n\n5:9 (first) +8 (second)=17 \u21927, carry1.\n\n6:8 (first) +9 (second)=17 \u21927, plus carry1 \u219218 \u21928, carry1.\n\n7:5 (first) +1 (second)=6 + carry1 \u21927, carry0.\n\n8:7 (first) +8 (second)=15 \u21925, carry1.\n\nFinal carryover1 \u2192 billions place.\n\nThus, the digits are:\n\nBillions:1,\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):5,\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):7,\n\nPosition6 (millions):8,\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands):7,\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):7,\n\nPosition3 (tho