rryover 1.\n\n8. Ten millions place:1 (first) +9 (second) =10, plus carryover 1 is 11. So write 1, carryover 1.\n\n9. Hundred millions place:1 (first) +1 (second) =2, plus carryover 1 is 3. Write 3. No more digits, so done.\n\nNow, the reversed result digits are: 9 6 9 4 6 0 4 1 3. Wait, let me list them in order:.\n\nStarting from the first digit (the ones place of the result):.\n\nDigits in reversed order (from the steps above):.\n\nFirst digit (position1):9.\n\nPosition2:6.\n\nPosition3:9.\n\nPosition4:4.\n\nPosition5:6.\n\nPosition6:0 (with a carryover).\n\nPosition7:4 (from 13+1=14, so 4 and carryover 1).\n\nPosition8:1 (from 10+1=11, so 1 and carryover 1).\n\nPosition9:3 (from 2+1=3 with the carryover).\n\nWait, but when we reversed the numbers, the first digit (position1) is the original ones, so the final sum's reversed digits are:.\n\n9 (position1),6,9,4,6,0,4,1,3 (position9). .\n\nSo to get the actual number, we reverse this list:.\n\nStarting from the last digit computed (the hundred millions place which is 3), then 1 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands?), wait let me check.\n\nWait, the reversed digits list is:.\n\nPosition1:9 (ones).\n\nPosition2:6 (tens).\n\nPosition3:9 (hundreds).\n\nPosition4:4 (thousands).\n\nPosition5:6 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition6:0 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition7:4 (millions).\n\nPosition8:1 (ten millions).\n\nPosition9:3 (hundred millions).\n\nSo the reversed digits are [9,6,9,4,6,0,4,1,3]. To get the actual number, we reverse this list:.\n\nStarting from the highest place (hundred millions):.\n\n3 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions),4 (millions),0 (hundred thousands),6 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),9 (hundreds),6 (tens),9 (ones). Wait, let me see:.\n\nWait the reversed digits list (the computed digits from right to left) is:.\n\nDigit 1: 9 (ones).\n\nDigit2:6 (tens).\n\nDigit3:9 (hundreds).\n\nDigit4:4 (thousands).\n\nDigit5:6 (ten thousands).\n\nDigit6:0 (hundred thousands).\n\nDigit7:4 (millions).\n\nDigit8