igit from right to left as we calculated:.\n\nStarting from the ones digit (position0):.\n\nPosition0:1.\n\nPosition1:0 (from 4+6 with carryover).\n\nPosition2:2 (from 4+7 +1 carryover).\n\nPosition3:5 (8+6 +1 carryover).\n\nPosition4:8 (3+4 +0).\n\nPosition5:1 (4+7 +0 carryover, but wait earlier step: position5 was 4+7=11 plus any carryover? Wait, let me check again step by step because I might have messed up the positions.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to go step by step again carefully. Maybe I made an error in the positions.\n\nWait, let me redo the addition step by step, carefully writing down each digit's addition with carryover. Let me write the numbers vertically:.\n\n          8 5 4 4 3 8 4 4 1.\n\n        + 4 4 5 7 4 6 7 6 0.\n\nBut actually, to align properly, let me write them digit by digit from right to left as positions 0 to 8.\n\nWait, perhaps the confusion is arising from the positions. Let me write them as:.\n\nFirst number: 854,438,441.\n\nBreaking down each digit from right (units) to left (hundred millions):.\n\nPosition 0: 1 (units).\n\nPosition 1: 4 (tens).\n\nPosition 2: 4 (hundreds).\n\nPosition 3: 8 (thousands).\n\nPosition 4: 3 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition 5: 4 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition 6: 5 (millions).\n\nPosition 7: 4 (ten millions).\n\nPosition 8: 8 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 445,746,760.\n\nBreaking down similarly:.\n\nPosition 0:0 (units).\n\nPosition 1:6 (tens).\n\nPosition 2:7 (hundreds).\n\nPosition 3:6 (thousands).\n\nPosition 4:4 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition 5:7 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition 6:5 (millions).\n\nPosition 7:4 (ten millions).\n\nPosition 8:4 (hundred millions).\n\nSo starting from position 0:.\n\nPosition0: 1 +0 =1. Write 1, carryover 0.\n\nPosition1:4 +6 =10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nPosition2:4 +7 =11 +1 (carryover) =12. Write 2, carryover1.\n\nPosition3:8 +6 =14 +1 =15. Write 5, carryover1.\n\nPosition4:3 +4 =7 +1 =8. Write 8, carryover0.\n\nPosition5:4 +7 =11 +0 =11. Write 1, carryover1.\n\nPositio