over into the billions place, so the total is 1,048,060,083.\n\nWait, but the user\'s answer was 1,048,010,083. Hmm, discrepancy here. Let me check each step again.\n\nLet me list each digit position with their place values:\n\nLet\'s write both numbers with their digits:\n\nFirst number: 2 6 7 5 9 4 9 8 6\n\nPositions (from right, starting at 1):\n\n1: 6 (ones)\n2: 8 (tens)\n3: 9 (hundreds)\n4: 4 (thousands)\n5: 9 (ten thousands)\n6: 5 (hundred thousands)\n7: 7 (millions)\n8: 6 (ten millions)\n9: 2 (hundred millions)\n\nSecond number:7 8 0 4 6 5 0 9 7\n\nSame positions:\n\n1:7 (ones)\n2:9 (tens)\n3:0 (hundreds)\n4:5 (thousands)\n5:6 (ten thousands)\n6:4 (hundred thousands)\n7:0 (millions)\n8:8 (ten millions)\n9:7 (hundred millions)\n\nAdding digit by digit from position 1 to 9:\n\nPosition 1 (ones):\n6 +7=13 → 3, carryover 1\n\nPosition 2 (tens):\n8 +9=17 +1=18 → 8, carryover1\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):\n9+0=9 +1=10 → 0, carryover1\n\nPosition4 (thousands):\n4+5=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):\n9 +6=15 +1=16 →6, carryover1\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):\n5+4=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1\n\nPosition7 (millions):\n7 +0=7 +1=8 →8, no carryover\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):\n6 +8=14 →4, carryover1\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):\n2+7=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1\n\nNow the final carryover1 is added to the next (billions) place, so the total is 1 followed by the digits we have:\n\nDigits from highest to lowest (billions, hundred millions, ten millions, ..., ones):\n\nBillions: 1\n\nHundred millions:0\n\nTen millions:4\n\nMillions:8\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nTen thousands:6\n\nThousands:0\n\nHundreds:8? Wait wait, let me see.\n\nWait, the digits obtained from each position:\n\nStarting from position1 (ones) to position9 (hundred millions):\n\nThe digits we wrote down are:\n\nPosition1:3\n\nPosition2:8\n\nPosition3:0\n\nPosition4:0\n\nPosition5:6\n\nPosition6:0\n\nPosition7:8\n\nPosition8:4\n\nPosition9:0\n\nPlus the carryover 1 in the billions place.\n\nSo arra