e second has a 0. 1 + 0 + 1 (carryover) = 2. So, 2 here. No carryover.\n\nMoving to the hundred millions place. The first number has an 8, and the second has an 8. 8 + 8 = 16. So, write 6 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the billions place. The first number has an 8, and the second has an 8. Adding those plus the carried-over 1: 8 + 8 + 1 = 17. So, we write 7 and carry over 1, but since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes another digit at the beginning</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
