 is 4. No carryover here.\n\nMillions place: 3 (from first number) + 4 (second number) = 7.\n\nTen millions place: 9 + 3 = 12. Wait, that's two digits. Hmm, so write 2 and carry over 1.\n\nHundred millions place: 3 + 4 = 7, plus the carried-over 1 makes 8</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
