p by step with their places:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\n1. Ones place: 7 + 4 = 11 → 1, carryover 1.\n2. Tens place: 2 + 7 = 9 + 1 (carryover) = 10 → 0, carryover 1.\n3. Hundreds place: 4 + 8 = 12 + 1 =13 → 3, carryover 1.\n4. Thousands place: 6 + 6 =12 +1 =13 →3, carryover1.\n5. Ten-thousands:4 +7=11 +1=12 →2, carryover1.\n6. Hundred-thousands:9 +3=12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n7. Millions:1 (from first number) +4 (from second) =5 +1=6 →6, no carryover.\n8. Ten-millions:1 +4 =5.\n9. Hundred-millions:2 +4=6.\n\nWait, but when I list them in order from ones to hundred-millions, the digits would be:.\n\nOnes:1.\n\nTens:0.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nThousands:3.\n\nTen-thousands:2.\n\nHundred-thousands:3.\n\nMillions:6.\n\nTen-millions:5.\n\nHundred-millions:6.\n\nSo writing the number from highest to lowest place, it's 6 (hundred-millions), 5 (ten-millions), 6 (millions), 3 (hundred-thousands), 2 (ten-thousands), 3 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 1 (ones). Wait, but that would be 656,323,301?.\n\nWait, let me check with actual addition:.\n\n211,964,427.\n\n+444,376,874.\n\nLet me add them step by step:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nFirst digit (units):.\n\n7 +4 =11 → 1, carryover 1.\n\nSecond digit (tens):.\n\n2 +7 =9 +1 =10 →0, carryover1.\n\nThird (hundreds):.\n\n4 +8 =12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nFourth (thousands):.\n\n6 +6 =12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nFifth (ten thousands):.\n\n4 +7 =11 +1=12 →2, carryover1.\n\nSixth (hundred thousands):.\n\n9 +3 =12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nSeventh (millions):.\n\n1 +4 =5 +1=6 →6.\n\nEighth (ten millions):.\n\n1 +4 =5.\n\nNinth (hundred millions):.\n\n2 +4 =6.\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nThe digits from right to left are 1 (units), 0 (tens), 3 (hundreds), 3 (thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 3 (hundred thousands), 6 (millions), 5 (ten millions), 6 (hundred millions). So when written left to right, it's 656,323,301.\n\nWait, let me confirm with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:.\n\n211,964,427 + 444,376,874.\n\nLet me break them into parts:.\n\n200,000,000 + 11,964,427.\n\n+ 400,000,000 + 44,376,874.\n\nAdding the millions first:.\n\n200,000,000 + 400,000,000 = 600,000,000.\n\nThen the rest: 11,964,427 +44,376,874.\n\nAdding those two:.\n\n11,964,427.\n\n+44,376,874.\n\n= ?.\n\n11,964,427 +44,376,874:.\n\nAdding units:.\n\n7+4=11 →1, carryover1.\n\n2+7=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1.\n\n4+6=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\n6+7=13 +1=14 →4, carryover1.\n\n9+3=12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\n1 (from 11,964,427's ten thousands place is 1 in the hundred thousands place? Wait, maybe I should do this step by step again.\n\nWait, perhaps an alternative way: 11,964,427 +44,376,874.\n\nLet me add them:.\n\n11,964,427.\n\n+44,376,874.\n\n= (11,000,000 + 964,427) + (44,000,000 + 376,874).\n\n= (11,000,000 +44,000,000) + (964,427 +376,874).\n\n=55,000,000 + (1,341,301) → because 964,427 +376,874.\n\nWait 964,427 + 376,874:.\n\nAdding the thousands:.\n\n427 + 874 = 1,301.\n\nThen 964,000 + 376,000 = 1,340,000.\n\nSo total 1,340,000 +1,301 = 1,341,301.\n\nTherefore total is 55,000,000 +1,341,301 =56,341,301</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
